{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon","id":1403808,"title":"Scion x WtA: Totem Spirit Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-21T07:27:00-07:00","id":1403808,"title":"Scion x WtA: Totem Spirit Pantheon","content":"This is just something I've been cooking with some friends for a few weeks now. It's probably not as accurate as it could be, but I wanted to portray the major Totem spirits from Werewolf: the Apocalypse as if they were Gods in Scion. There's two ways for them to be utilized:<br /> <br /> 1. As a complete pantheon, with the Fera and the Garou especially as their followers and a Fera-focused Pantheon Purview<br /> 2. As supplemental Gods for the other pantheons they share territory with (Pegasus with the Theoi, Owl with the Netjer, etc.)<br /> 3. As a combination of the two.<br /> <br /> I've gone with option 3 by default, having the Totems serve as a full pantheon but with each pantheon purview of the land they live in. I haven't created a specific purview as of yet, but I'll try when I have the time. For the mean time, this is what I have thus far:<br /> <br /> Virtues: <b>Man</b> vs. <b>Wolf</b> (<b>Man</b> represents the human element, the innovator, the part of the Garou that communicates with reason and measure. However, it is also within Man's nature to tame, corrupt and exploit what he can for his own gain. <b>Wolf</b> represents the spiritual element, the wild thing, the part which embraces nature's chaos and feels the subtle flows of the spirit world. However, it is also the part which <i>destroys</i> things, whether for sustenance, renown or for no reason at all.<br /> <br /> Asset Skills: Close Combat, Survival<br /> <br /> <b>Pegasus</b>, Totem of the Black Furies<ul><li>Callings: Guardian, Judge, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (4): Beasts (Horses), Journeys, Metamorphosis, Sky</li> </ul><b>Rat</b>, Totem of the Bone Gnawers and the Ratkin<ul><li>Callings: Lover, Trickster, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Rat, Insects), Death, Deception, Epic Stamina, War</li> </ul><b>Unicorn</b>, Totem of the Children of Gaia<ul><li>Callings: Healer, Lover, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (7): Beasts (Horses), Epic Dexterity, Health, Journeys, Order, Passion (Serenity), Wild</li> </ul><b>Stag</b>, Totem of the Fianna<ul><li>Callings: Creator, Hunter, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (6): Artistry (Singing), Beasts (Deer), Fertility, Fortune, Geasa, Wild</li> </ul><b>Fenris</b>, Totem of the Get<ul><li>Callings: Judge, Warrior, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Wolves), Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, War, Wyrd</li> </ul><b>Cockroach</b>, Totem of the Glass Walkers<ul><li>Callings: Creator, Sage, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (6): Beasts (Cockroaches, Spiders), Epic Dexterity, Forge, Order, Prosperity, Sky</li> </ul><b>Griffin</b>, Totem of the Red Talons<ul><li>Callings: Hunter, Liminal, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (4): Beasts (Raptors, Wolves), Chaos, Passion (Rage, Fear), Wild</li> </ul><b>Grandfather Thunder</b>, Totem of the Shadow Lords<ul><li>Callings: Judge, Leader, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (7): Beasts (Crows), Darkness, Deception, Order, Passion (Fear), Prosperity, Sky</li> </ul><b>Owl</b>, Totem of the Silent Striders<ul><li>Callings: Liminal, Trickster, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Owls), Death, Heku, Journeys, Stars</li> </ul><b>Falcon</b>, Totem of the Silver Fangs<ul><li>Callings: Leader, Lover, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Falcons), Moon, Order, Passion (Courage), Prosperity</li> </ul><b>Chimera</b>, Totem of the Stargazers<ul><li>Callings: Liminal, Sage, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (7): Chaos, Deception, Epic Dexterity, Fortune, Journeys, Stars, Yoga</li> </ul><b>Uktena</b>, the Older Brother<ul><li>Callings: Guardian, Sage, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (7): Beasts (Serpents), Darkness, Deception, Dodaem, Earth, Fortune, Water</li> </ul><b>Wendigo</b>, the Younger Brother<ul><li>Callings: Hunter, Warrior, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (7): Death, Dodaem, Fire, Frost, Passion (Hunger, Rage), Sky, Water</li> </ul>Titans: The Fera recognize 3 Titans as pertaining to them. Depending on the type of Fera or their Tribe, they either support, tolerate or despise any one of these three:<ul><li>The Wyld, the spirit of creation and chaos, is currently the weakest of the Triat due to the predations of the other two members. The Black Furies and Red Talons praise this Titan the most. Purview: Chaos. Virtues: Fecundity, Rapacity.</li> <li>The Weaver, the spirit of order and form. She is said to have been the first to go mad in her grief over countless destroyed creations, and has tried to imprison the Wyrm to prevent further death. She is revered by the Glass Walkers, which is regarded by some as blasphemous. Purview: Order. Virtues: Submission, Dominance.</li> <li>The Wyrm, the spirit of destruction and corruption. He fell into madness after enduring imprisonment from the Weaver for an unknown amount of time. While none of the official Tribes view him in any high regard, his Titan cult, the Black Spiral Dancers, revere him to no end. Purview: Death. Virtues: Dominance, Rapacity.</li> </ul>Primordial: <b>Luna</b><br /> Callings: Hunter, Liminal, Trickster<br /> Purviews: Beasts, Chaos, Metamorphosis, Moon<br /> <br /> The &quot;official&quot; Primordial of the Fera, Luna, the Spirit of the Moon, has waxed and waned in power over time, much like the moon does in it's phases. At times, she has been beholden to the Triat, and others, she reigns supreme over them. However, regardless of where the tides may be, it is unquestioned that she is more powerful than any of the Totems of the Fera, thus, she remains in this position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","user":"Critian Caceorte","date":". 07-26-2020, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T14:46:11-07:00","id":1403888,"title":"","content":"I love this. but I think the primordial should be gaia, not luna. <br /> <br /> and do you mind if I write some titanspawn. you know, the spirit minions of the triat, as well as the incarna of the wyrm and weaver? and other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T23:13:49-07:00","id":1403948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1403888#post1403888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this. but I think the primordial should be gaia, not luna.<br /> <br /> and do you mind if I write some titanspawn. you know, the spirit minions of the triat, as well as the incarna of the wyrm and weaver? and other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why Gaia would be considered, I just wasn't sure if she was already a Primordial for the Theoi. I might add her as an &quot;optional&quot; variant for ST's.<br /> <br /> As for the titanspawn, sure! I was planning to write up Whipoorwill myself since I forgot about it in my initial write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T00:42:13-07:00","id":1403955,"title":"","content":"This is great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T03:30:23-07:00","id":1403969,"title":"","content":"I was big into this in first ed Scion, I had the Celestial Incarna Pantheon and the Tribal Totem Pantheon. Good Onya!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:21:14-07:00","id":1404016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1403948#post1403948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why Gaia would be considered, I just wasn't sure if she was already a Primordial for the Theoi. I might add her as an &quot;optional&quot; variant for ST's.<br /> <br /> As for the titanspawn, sure! I was planning to write up Whipoorwill myself since I forgot about it in my initial write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>alright. banes and other wyrm minions will come soon. as will weaver minions. wyld spirits will not be considered titanspawn because the garou don't consider the wyld a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:28:26-07:00","id":1404018,"title":"","content":"sorry to double post so soon, but I just figured a work around for gaia, if you don't make her optional. <br /> <br /> I am pretty sure that yama, god of the underworld, is a member of four different pantheons. if one god can be in four pantheons at once, I am pretty sure a primordial can be in two. also, Fenris is a part of the asier. admittedly as a titan (I think), but he is a part of the norse gods. <br /> <br /> alright, I will wait a few hours (or more) then make an overview post on the fallen breeds (the wyrm corrupted fera).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:59:58-07:00","id":1404038,"title":"","content":"By popular demand, here is Gaia depicted as a Primordial Goddess:<br /> Callings: Creator, Healer, Hunter<br /> Purviews: Beasts, Earth, Fertility, Water, Wild<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's Whippoorwill depicted as a &quot;God&quot; for the Black Spiral Dancers:<br /> <b>Whippoorwill</b>, Totem of the Black Spiral<ul><li>Callings: Hunter, Trickster, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (6): Beasts (Birds), Death, Deception, Epic Stamina, Fire, Health</li> </ul><br /> And here is a facet of him as a titanspawn:<br /> Facet of Whippoorwill<br /> Archetype: Titanspawn<br /> Drive: To promote its own self-importance<br /> Qualities: Incorporeality, Vulnerability (Silver), Flight, Baleful Touch<br /> Flairs: Illusions, Sorcery (Beasts (Birds))<br /> Primary Pool (13): Flying, Spinning Lies<br /> Secondary Pool (11): Singing, Stealth<br /> Desperation Pool (7)<br /> Health: 8<br /> Defense: 3<br /> Initiative: 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T11:48:55-07:00","id":1404062,"title":"","content":"ok, I am working on the wyrm overview, but my contributions are gonna be pure fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T15:05:32-07:00","id":1404102,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Gaia and Luna both being Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T15:44:24-07:00","id":1404109,"title":"","content":"You could weave in the Mages and Changelings. Make the founders of each of the Sidhe Houses a God, but not all of the Faerie Gods. The Oracles of Mage could have achieved demigod status and be on the way to being full gods, or simply say the Oracles are Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T20:13:28-07:00","id":1404161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1404109#post1404109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could weave in the Mages and Changelings. Make the founders of each of the Sidhe Houses a God, but not all of the Faerie Gods. The Oracles of Mage could have achieved demigod status and be on the way to being full gods, or simply say the Oracles are Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also working on an Antediluvian Pantheon right now. Changelings are possible, though heavily Celtic so they might as well just be parts of the Tuatha. Mages... I mean... you could? My issue with doing the Oracles is the same issue I had when I had the random idea to make a <i>Proxy</i> pantheon from Trinity Continuum: There is just not a ton of info available to really draw from. What callings could I use for so-and-so when at most they have like a paragraph of background? The Totem spirits at least have their Tribes to draw inspiration for their Purviews, that's how I came up with most of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T02:16:04-07:00","id":1404208,"title":"","content":"My 1st ed game was set in the World of Darkness, it was so fun. But the Rules were so bad in 1st ed, and it unravels real quick outside of hero.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T17:13:42-07:00","id":1404321,"title":"","content":"I don't really feel like going through all of the W:tA fetishes, but the least I can do is add the Klaives, there's a conspicuous hole without them:<br /> <br /> Klaive (****)<br /> Purview: War<br /> Motif: Blessed Silver dipped and stained in Honor<br /> +2se to convince target to engage in a (lethal) duel, +1se to attack with Klaive<br /> Weapon Tags: Lethal, Melee, Thrown (0), Versatile, Piercing (2), Aggravated (2)<br /> Flaws: Must imbue a Dot of Legend to function (5)<br /> <br /> Grand Klaive (*****)<br /> Purview: War, ANY<br /> Motif: Blessed Silver meant for the Greatest of Champions<br /> +2se to attack with Grand Klaive, +1se to demonstrate honor<br /> Weapon Tags: Lethal, Melee, Two-Handed, Unconcealable, Aggravated (2), Piercing (2), Versatile (2)<br /> Flaws: Must imbue a Dot of Legend to function (5), Reduce one tag\u2019s numerical at the end of a scene in which the virtue [Wolf] was not fulfilled, full functionality restored once [Wolf] is fulfilled. (3)<br /> <br /> The reason I added the Dot imbuement as a flaw was to serve as a parallel for the loss of Gnosis when you wield a klaive in W:tA. Felt that it was the most relevant option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T14:34:36-07:00","id":1404458,"title":"","content":"Quick Question for everyone: For the next thing in this Pantheon, should I focus on other Birthright stuff, or in-depth God descriptions and incarnations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","user":"Critian Caceorte","date":". 07-24-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T16:13:40-07:00","id":1404663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1404458#post1404458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question for everyone: For the next thing in this Pantheon, should I focus on other Birthright stuff, or in-depth God descriptions and incarnations?</div> </div> </div> </div>in depth god stuff. <br /> <br /> also, heres my overview for the wyrm itself. <br /> <br /> The wyrm <br /> Of the triat (what the totem pantheon call there titans) there is one that all there official followers can agree must be fought. The wyrm is what Apophis is to the Netjer, or what the various star demons are to the teotl. But it was not always this way.<br /> Once the wyrm, and the trait at large, were peaceful. Once they existed in harmony, and the changing breeds (the garou and fera) had no problems with titanspawn or even titanic hostility. But then the weaver had an existential crisis and went mad. She tricked the wyrm and imprisoned him in the pattern web, the torture of which caused the horrible Corrupter Wyrm to arise. A tulpa of titanic scale, in both power and size, whenever the totem pantheon and its followers refer to the wyrm they fight they are referring to the corrupter wyrm.<br /> Where the balance wyrm was a massive serpent, the corrupter wyrm is a hydra. Indeed, it is split into many heads, each of which is a rival with the others. The heads are divided into three types, the first being the triatic wyrms. These heads are physical (or at least as physical as spirits can be) and have minds, each is a corrupted representation of the triat. The second category is the urge wyrms, which lack physicality but spread dark emotions. The urge wyrms are insidious and lurk in every heart that feels there emotion, pushing healthy negative feelings to the point of mania. The final type of head are the elemental wyrms, which are purely physical and lack minds. They are four in total, each embodying a wyrm element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:41:06-07:00","id":1404722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1404663#post1404663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> in depth god stuff.<br /> <br /> also, heres my overview for the wyrm itself.<br /> <br /> The wyrm<br /> Of the triat (what the totem pantheon call there titans) there is one that all there official followers can agree must be fought. The wyrm is what Apophis is to the Netjer, or what the various star demons are to the teotl. But it was not always this way.<br /> Once the wyrm, and the trait at large, were peaceful. Once they existed in harmony, and the changing breeds (the garou and fera) had no problems with titanspawn or even titanic hostility. But then the weaver had an existential crisis and went mad. She tricked the wyrm and imprisoned him in the pattern web, the torture of which caused the horrible Corrupter Wyrm to arise. A tulpa of titanic scale, in both power and size, whenever the totem pantheon and its followers refer to the wyrm they fight they are referring to the corrupter wyrm.<br /> Where the balance wyrm was a massive serpent, the corrupter wyrm is a hydra. Indeed, it is split into many heads, each of which is a rival with the others. The heads are divided into three types, the first being the triatic wyrms. These heads are physical (or at least as physical as spirits can be) and have minds, each is a corrupted representation of the triat. The second category is the urge wyrms, which lack physicality but spread dark emotions. The urge wyrms are insidious and lurk in every heart that feels there emotion, pushing healthy negative feelings to the point of mania. The final type of head are the elemental wyrms, which are purely physical and lack minds. They are four in total, each embodying a wyrm element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall, decent, however there are a few typos and the later part of the explanation doesn't seem to flow that well. I can't quite put my finger on it at the moment, I'll take a deeper look at it later.<br /> <br /> With that said, here are 3 of the in-depth descriptions I've written so far. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Pegasus, Totem of the Black Furies</b><br /> Hear the tale of Pegasus! After the death of the last Gorgon, Luna, in the guise of Artemis, created a protector spirit to guard the Black Furies and to temper their rage before it could spill out onto the rest of the world. An equine creature modeled after Poseidon\u2019s invention but also granted a set of wind-catching wings, his power left many envious, including Athena herself. With the assistance of the hero Bellerophon, they captured Pegasus and made him a mere mount, a tool for Bellerophon\u2019s achievements. It was only after being gelded by his would-be rider that Pegasus had enough, and tossed the man off of his back to die from the fall.<br /> Ever since this incident, Pegasus has served as an advocate for women, as well as those rare few men who became sterile via injury, and counts them among his Chosen if he judges them worthy. He is also known to Create some Scions out of horses that have been abused and mistreated by their owners. Due to his injury, he is unable to have direct progeny, though he does not waste his time dwelling on such a subject. In those times he takes on a human Incarnation, his selves are either disfigured men, transgender individuals or, rarely, women. All are involved in some form of agriculture or military career, and are noteworthy for their disdain for cruel \u201ctraditional\u201d methods of animal care.<br /> His tribe are the Black Furies, a group of women, both Garou and not, who band together to combat the predations of Man. While they are often stereotyped by outsiders as raging misandrists, their main focus is on the protection of women, rather than the harming of men. Under Pegasus\u2019 direction, the tribe accepts all women who seek shelter there, and kicks out all men once they are of age, however there are some men raised in the tribe, such as the Metis, who were born sterile, and are thus allowed to remain. While sterile men from outside of the tribe are technically allowed in as well, they must prove to be above any sort of hate for womankind if they hope to retain their place. Should any who dedicate themselves to him be cruel to women for no good reason, Pegasus casts them out into the dirt for their hypocrisy.<ul><li>Callings: Guardian, Judge, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (4): Beasts (Horses), Journeys, Metamorphosis, Sky</li> </ul><b>Rat, Totem of the Bone Gnawers</b><br /> There is no tale to tell for the Totem of the Bone Gnawers, the God of Rodents and Disease. No spirit, save Chimera, is as amorphous and changing as Rat is. Regarded by some as a male God of War and Plagues, and others as a caring Mother Goddess, there are many facets to Rat\u2019s character, so much so that it\u2019s difficult to keep track of all of them. This is not helped by a largely obscure backstory with conflicting details, where there are any. Because of this, the tale of Rat cannot accurately be told. But, perhaps\u2026 that\u2019s just how Rat wants it.<br /> Out of all the totems, Rat prefers Born Scions the most, though the \u201chow\u201d in accomplishing this is not always moral, or even legal. Though never a rapist in his male assortment of forms, as a woman Rat has been known to extort high-profile targets with the fact of her pregnancy, while in other Incarnations she raises loving families with poor endearing men. Because of the risk in guessing wrong with which Incarnation embodies which aspect, many foreign Gods have decided to avoid \u201csticking their dick in crazy\u201d as a safety precaution. Hardly anyone can blame them when taking into account a mainstay of Rat\u2019s incarnations besides children: Diseases. Whether this be an office worker with a perpetual cough, or a bug chaser looking to knock an illness off the bucket list, Rat is disgusting. Filthy. Just as Rat wishes to be.<br /> Nearly all of Rat\u2019s Scions, save for the Incarnations, receive their \u201cVisitation\u201d in the form of a sickness known as the Birthing Plague. Rather than being selective in which of his children have their divine heritage awakened, she instead puts them through a trial by fire, with those who die of the Plague obviously not being worthy enough, and those who survive receive newfound strength as is their right. Even among the other Totem spirits this practice is quite contentious, to say nothing of how other Pantheons view it. Many of her children understandably hate his guts, even as they enjoy their Gifts. Beyond this, her children tend to be so varied in terms of appearance and personality as to not even be identifiable, except for a high resistance to illness in adulthood.<br /> Rat\u2019s tribe, the Bone Gnawers, don\u2019t tend to focus on Rat\u2019s disease aspect as his critics do. Instead, they focus on her cunning, battle prowess and just overall survivability. Treated as garbage by many, they embrace this image in order to recruit new members. Falcon may be exceptionally picky about who joins his tribe, but just about anyone fits right in with the Rat pack. Just don\u2019t mention being a Scion of Owl, those two have some bad blood going back millennia.<ul><li>Callings: Lover, Trickster, Therianthrope</li> </ul><ul><li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Rat, Insects), Death, Deception, Epic Stamina, War</li> </ul><b>Fenris, Totem of the Get</b><br /> Hear the tale of Great Fenris! He who was one of the first, and the greatest, of the Garou, who battled that bastard Odin and made him flee in fear! While every other Garou founder has disappeared into the eroding river of history, he alone stands firm and strong. Though greatest among his kindred, he refused to take a wife who could not prove herself to be his equal in strength and character. This left him to wallow in loneliness for countless years until a chance encounter in battle would provide a glimpse to his future spouse, Sigun. Though they fell for each other quickly enough, Sigun was already promised to another, and so Fenris challenged her prospective husband, a Jotun, to single combat for her hand. Was it any surprise that he won? Long after the two had wedded and had children, the Gallows-God, Odin, was tricked into razing Heimhalla itself and killing Sigun for fear of Fenris\u2019 power, to which the Great Wolf responded by pursuing Odin\u2019s demise for the rest of time.<br /> Even today, the Aesir and their spawn fear the might of Fenris. They portray him as Titanspawn, and seek to ruin his reputation with other pantheons by promoting this image. Not like any besides the idiots among the Yazata and the Tuatha actually believe them, of course, they\u2019re smarter than that. Great Fenris does not care for such false claims, not when action speaks far more than words. When he acts, he does so at his full strength, with no quarter given to his opponents. In the World, he takes the form of soldiers, police, athletes, or any other kind of \u201cstrong\u201d archetype or career. He Choses individuals which demonstrate an inner strength, not necessarily an outer one, that can\u2019t be questioned. Those that falter, he turns away from, injures or even kills. While he is a Wolf, he does not uplift these as Created Scions as often as you might expect, though it\u2019s not unheard of for him to do so. He also does not have direct children, refusing to have any child with a woman who is not as strong and willful as Sigun was, quite the challenge for the average woman. Uniquely among the Totems, he produces the greatest amount of Incarnation Scions, due to his origin as one of the first Werewolves.<br /> He presides over the Get, a tribe of strength devotees who occupy Scandinavia and venerate the Great Wolf. While not as muscle-brained as some make them out to be, they have had a history of misogyny which has only been purged recently, and some say not fully. Beyond this, they are exceptionally judgemental of others in regards to their strength, and are even more so towards themselves. Before any individual can be considered a tribe member, even the kids of one, they must pass various trials to demonstrate both inner and outer strength. In the case that they are accepted, the tests become subdued, more to temper the member\u2019s spirit rather than find his flaws. Climbing up the ranks requires further tests to ensure that whatever chips in the armor there were are fixed or at least being worked upon. No matter one\u2019s position, however, all heed the Great Wolf\u2019s decree: If any refuse a worthy fight, they can, and must, leave the tribe immediately.<ul><li>Callings: Judge, Warrior, Therianthrope</li> <li>Purviews (5): Beasts (Wolves), Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, War, Wyrd</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T20:49:39-07:00","id":1405014,"title":"","content":"I like it, but why do the <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yazata and the Tuatha believe the aseir's claims? also, maybe there is a titan that claims the name of Fenris, and is the father of the Fenrir. maybe Garm (I think that's his name) is the treacherious first son of Fenris and is responsible for the Fenrir, the bas reputation of Fenris himself, and is the one who kills tyr and then Odin at R</span></span>agnarok before getting killed by Vidar.<br /> <br /> also, I am still working on the wyrmish stuff, I just felt put on the spot by your creation of <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Whippoorwill, so I posted the only part I had finished. my original plan was a megapost detailing an overview of the wyrm, the black spiral dancers, the fallen and mockery breeds, pentex, wyrm cults, banes and fomori. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T21:40:57-07:00","id":1405018,"title":"","content":"I would say the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 would likely be very quick to believe that any and every wolf is evil and awful. Medieval Ireland (the culture that produced the T\u00faatha D\u00e9) had <i>thoughts</i> about wolves. Mostly that they were forces of degenerate disorder that were solitary creatures that killed to feed perpetual hungers. The term <i>C\u00fa</i> (Hound, Wolf) is used as an element of a large number of warrior names (Conall Cernach, Conchobar, Connla, C\u00fa Chulainn) which is representative of their role as dangerous people who as often lash out at society and betray it as often as support it. The term <i>C\u00fa Glas</i>, 'Grey Hound' or 'Wolf' is a legal term applied to outsiders who have low status, or one applied to people who commit the two most heinous crimes under their legal system, <i>fingal</i>, 'kinslaying,' and incest.<br /> <br /> However, the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 are actually very good at... lets say 'breaking' wolves. Ireland under good kingship renders wolves as docile creatures.<br /> <br /> Don't know how much that would influence what you're working on here, but if you want to find ways to fit this into the broader setting of Scion, things like this may be helpful. The Fomori might be a challenge though as the Fomori from Werewolf and from actual Irish sagas are like... the only common feature is the name. You might want to make it just being two different groups that have the same name rather than connecting them.<br /> <br /> (Also as a note about the Yazata, they are beings of ultimate truth. If this guy isn't a Titan they would never in a million years be fooled into a lie to believe he was. The Yazata are righteous, not stupid or cruel.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-28-2020, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T21:59:27-07:00","id":1405020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405014#post1405014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, but why do the <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yazata and the Tuatha believe the aseir's claims? also, maybe there is a titan that claims the name of Fenris, and is the father of the Fenrir. maybe Garm (I think that's his name) is the treacherious first son of Fenris and is responsible for the Fenrir, the bas reputation of Fenris himself, and is the one who kills tyr and then Odin at R</span></span>agnarok before getting killed by Vidar.<br /> <br /> also, I am still working on the wyrmish stuff, I just felt put on the spot by your creation of <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Whippoorwill, so I posted the only part I had finished. my original plan was a megapost detailing an overview of the wyrm, the black spiral dancers, the fallen and mockery breeds, pentex, wyrm cults, banes and fomori. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yazata are describe in canon as being extremely Titan-ist. If a person or group <i>could </i>be a Titan or Titanspawn, then they must be. I have no doubt that them hearing even a rumor from the Aesir, who they get along okay with, about Fenris being the Titan(spawn) Fenrir, they'd believe it.<br /> 2. The Tuatha are good friends with the Aesir, but they wouldn't necessarily go after Fenris even if he was a Titan, they've had better relations with Titans in the past than others.<br /> 3. It's certainly possible, though this being Scion, the answers could be all or none of the above.<br /> 4. Don't feel intimidated by what I've done, just post what you wish! This is supposed to be more of a communal thing, so the more people involved the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T00:30:24-07:00","id":1405029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1404722#post1404722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even today, the Aesir and their spawn fear the might of Fenris. They portray him as Titanspawn, and seek to ruin his reputation with other pantheons by promoting this image. Not like any besides the idiots among the Yazata and the Tuatha actually believe them, of course, they\u2019re smarter than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Maybe</i> don't refer to the Divinities of a very real (and still practiced) religion, as Idiots in favor of a made up version of an antagonist from a different Pantheon, turned character from a different game entirely, and imply that all the other Pantheons (including this fictional one) are smarter than them, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-28-2020, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T01:24:00-07:00","id":1405030,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Yazata are Righteous, but I imagine that they would prefer to make up their own minds about whether someone or something is <i>druj</i>.<br /> <br /> And even if a figure is titan-ish, i believe that many of them would be willing to try and show a being the truth of <i>Asha</i> before condemning them.<br /> <br /> Y'know, maybe do a bit more reading of the Yazata before you try and smear them as gullible Lawful Stupid crusaders. Remember, people actually worship these Gods, in our world. I know one of the writers of the 2e Yazata worships them. So maybe show a pinch of basic respect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T04:00:27-07:00","id":1405045,"title":"","content":"ok, the rest of my wyrm post will be in the megapost format, and I have made good progress on the overview of banes. <br /> <br /> also, while I don't really know much about 2ed, I am pretty sure one of the main rules is that all myths are true, with different cosmologies explaining away contridictions. the only way the Fenris of norse mythology, who is the son of loki and Angrboda, bound by gleipnir in the middle of Lake Amsvartnir, and this Fenris who is clearly a god and makes his home in the tribal homeland of the get of Fenris, cause I see the umbra realms of WTA being the totem spirit pantheon cosmology, is that they are two different individuals. <br /> <br /> here's how I see it playing out; garm is the wolf son of Loki and Angrboda, and by this time Fenris is a god. His rivalry with Odin causes him to adopt Garm as his son, and he dosent think much of what happens after. Garm decides to take the name Fenris, and is called the False Fenris by everyone who dosent belive the Asier's lies. It was he who was bound by the Gleipnir, and he who fathered the Fenrir. When Ragnarok comes he will break his chains and devour the sun and moon, and then kill his sons who get angry at there father for stealing there eternal prey. he will then kill tyr and finish his rampage by killing odin, before then getting killed by Vidar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T04:08:01-07:00","id":1405046,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t worry on contradicting the other myths too. Kronos (The Titan) is at same time locked in Tartarus and helping people with seasonal issues, and it\u2019s the same religion/myth, the first as the Greeks see (Kronus) and the second as Romans do (Saturn).<br /> <br /> Ferins can be both a Titan and a God at same time, and be locked waiting to start Ragnarock and helping Werewolves to fight Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T06:00:10-07:00","id":1405054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405046#post1405046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t worry on contradicting the other myths too. Kronos (The Titan) is at same time locked in Tartarus and helping people with seasonal issues, and it\u2019s the same religion/myth, the first as the Greeks see (Kronus) and the second as Romans do (Saturn).<br /> <br /> Ferins can be both a Titan and a God at same time, and be locked waiting to start Ragnarock and helping Werewolves to fight Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>well I didn't know that. but I still like the idea of a false Fenris. However I will subscribe to your idea, cause it allows the myths to happen as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":".  original phrasing repetitive 07-28-2020, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T06:11:03-07:00","id":1405055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405046#post1405046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t worry on contradicting the other myths too. Kronos (The Titan) is at same time locked in Tartarus and helping people with seasonal issues, and it\u2019s the same religion/myth, the first as the Greeks see (Kronus) and the second as Romans do (Saturn).<br /> <br /> Ferins can be both a Titan and a God at same time, and be locked waiting to start Ragnarock and helping Werewolves to fight Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilariously Kronos <i>isn't</i> locked up... Zeus lets him (and if the scraps of Prometheus Unbound are to be believed, all the imprisoned male Titans) out like two paragraphs after their defeat to rule Elysium <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm pretty certain Atlas is the only person still suffering for that kerfuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T15:25:43-07:00","id":1405102,"title":"","content":"So, after double checking the respective sections of the Core rulebook and the supplements, I must apologize for an error I made in my research. I had confused the Yazata and the Deva's attitudes towards the Titans (the Deva's being the fanatics, and the Yazata being more mixed), which resulted in me making statements about the Yazata which were not true (something they'd probably find especially egregious.) I will be correcting this error in the final version of the in-depth God descriptions. <br /> <br /> As for the conflict in legends between Fenris and Fenrir, thank you for your suggestions! I will still keep the idea that <i>Fenris</i> and his followers believe that the Aesir are spreading rumors and lies, even if the Aesir themselves don't think so. It's a canonical belief from the Get of Fenris tribe book, and it helps to create a conflict between the two that can be exploited for storytelling. Generating more of these pantheon interactions, especially with those Totems who share a pantheon like Pegasus, is especially important for this project. How does [Insert Totem Here] feel about so-and-so? Or vice versa? Any suggestions for stuff like this is more than welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T16:15:05-07:00","id":1405105,"title":"","content":"Remember: If all they have in common is a name, sometimes you can get away with going &quot;Also, they're not related to [Other figure] and are very tired with the mix-ups.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Also most of the Deva would probably at least hear another Pantheon out. Like, Durga takes no pleasure in the many MANY Asura she's killed, and would undoubtedly accept any surrender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-28-2020, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T16:43:30-07:00","id":1405107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405102#post1405102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after double checking the respective sections of the Core rulebook and the supplements, I must apologize for an error I made in my research. I had confused the Yazata and the Deva's attitudes towards the Titans (the Deva's being the fanatics, and the Yazata being more mixed), which resulted in me making statements about the Yazata which were not true (something they'd probably find especially egregious.) I will be correcting this error in the final version of the in-depth God descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear I don't think calling the Deva Idiots is going to be an improvement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T18:15:36-07:00","id":1405109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405107#post1405107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear I don't think calling the Deva Idiots is going to be an improvement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well fanatic isn't the same as idiot. Perhaps explaining that our ancient foes have a name that sounds like yours. And your ancient foes have a name that sounds like ours. We think that this is a trick they've pulled on both of us to have us fight to their advantage. Let's start diplomatic relations and break out of this trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T18:58:50-07:00","id":1405112,"title":"","content":"I admit if I were to make a fictional Pantheon, I probably wouldn't mention their relations with other Pantheons if I didn't have to. Mostly because I'd be assuming history and context I don't have which makes me feel cautious. So I'd probably focus on them being their own thing, and mostly keeping to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T21:33:23-07:00","id":1405126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405112#post1405112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit if I were to make a fictional Pantheon, I probably wouldn't mention their relations with other Pantheons if I didn't have to. Mostly because I'd be assuming history and context I don't have which makes me feel cautious. So I'd probably focus on them being their own thing, and mostly keeping to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in most circumstances, I'd agree. However, many of the Totem spirits (Pegasus, Fenris, etc.) have <i>direct</i> connections to deities from other pantheons (Pegasus with Athena, and Artemis, Fenris with Odin and Loki, etc.). Because of that, saying &quot;let's not include other pantheons&quot; just isn't going to work, because then you're erasing the legends those individuals have. And without the history, they're just not as interesting. Well, maybe Fenris, but Pegasus? Without Athena and Bellerophon he is never tamed, and without Bellerophon he doesn't get castrated like he does in WtA. This isn't even getting into Stag's connection to the Fianna, which is more Irish than leprechauns ever were, Chimera which as a creature is involved in several mythologies, and Wendigo who's... you know, <i>Wendigo. </i>And for the final cherry on the cake, the two big universal figures in the pantheon are <i>Luna</i> and <i><b>Gaia.</b></i> Like it or not, White Wolf created connections to these mythologies, connections that have yet to be changed in the past 30~ years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T01:12:07-07:00","id":1405140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405126#post1405126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Wendigo who's... you know, <i>Wendigo. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually suggest very much cutting off any connection between this entity and the Manitou villains, since A. The Wendigo are a whole collection of monsters, not a single individual, so &quot;Wendigo... Who's Wendigo&quot; doesn't make sense to begin with and B. Wendigo are supposed to be the worst monsters of a First Nations Culture, with no possibility of redemption once they've crossed over into full Wendigo-hood... Taking that and turning it into a Patron option for Protagonists has many unfortunate implications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT : As an aside, the Uktena is Cherokee, not Ojibwe, so it really shouldn't have the Manitou PSP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-29-2020, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T02:35:11-07:00","id":1405145,"title":"","content":"Just as a heads-up, even with you meaning Dev\u00e1 and not Yazata, I would recommend to be careful around labels like &quot;idiots&quot;. The Yazata are not some quaint fantasy religion once worshipped in the past, their worshippers still exist and are persecuted in multiple states for our continued worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T02:55:08-07:00","id":1405149,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be honest: the usage of Wendigo and Uktena as patrons, does disturb me and this attitude applies to the source material as well. This is a prime excuse to change the names, and remove the offensive stereotyping of Native people tied to that, I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll still work fine if you change those two names \ud83d\ude03. And yeah I\u2019m with Manus and Samudra, presenting the gods of real life religions, ones that have historically and presently oppression, as idiots is objectionable on basic principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:31:09-07:00","id":1405165,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with most of the concerns others have raised here. I think building a pantheon based in part on the fictionalised portrayal of real world cultures and mythologies isn't impossible in itself, but it definitely requires some special care. Personally, I think if you are interested in incorporating WtA into Scion, that might actually be a good opportunity to rework its lore into something that fits, you know, actual mythology. Let's face it, White Wolf was never that interested in portraying mythology beyond some superficial allusions. That may be enough for the World of Darkness, but it clashes with everything Scion is about. So I would say the first step of adapting WtA lore to Scion is to figure out where their fiction overlaps with real world cultures, investigate if there are any issues with their portrayal (and there probably are), and try to adapt the fiction to fit the actual mythology. For instance, I can see Fenris being <i>both</i> a Titan feared by the Aesir and a God worshipped by the Garou. Because guess what: a great, man- and god-eating wolf is terrifying for men and gods, but for wolves he's awesome and deserving of worship. The goal would be to fit those two parts together in a way that doesn't invalidate the Aesir's side of the story.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a less research-heavy approach might be to make it very clear that your write-ups (or at least the ones that touch on real world myth) aren't objective facts about the nature of the World but unreliable narration from the perspective of the Garou. Every pantheon has its own view of the world and they perceive elements of foreign cosmologies through their own 'lense'. Emphasise that lense and point to moments where it is incomplete or even contradicted when faced with other mythologies. So, for instance, the Garou might <i>claim </i>that Artemis is an Incarnation of Luna but the Theoi disagree. Similarly, many Garou might be angry that people like the Ojibwe demonise them as inhuman monsters... until they encounter an <i>actual</i> Ojibwe Wendigo for the first time and realise that, yes, these monsters definitely exist, they are clearly Titanspawn/corrupted by the Wyrm/fallen to Rage and Hunger, and they are exactly as monstrous and irredeemable as the Ojibwe have always said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":25842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","user":"Mr Wopsle","date":". 07-29-2020, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:46:59-07:00","id":1405169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405140#post1405140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would actually suggest very much cutting off any connection between this entity and the Manitou villains, since A. The Wendigo are a whole collection of monsters, not a single individual, so &quot;Wendigo... Who's Wendigo&quot; doesn't make sense to begin with and B. Wendigo are supposed to be the worst monsters of a First Nations Culture, with no possibility of redemption once they've crossed over into full Wendigo-hood... Taking that and turning it into a Patron option for Protagonists has many unfortunate implications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT : As an aside, the Uktena is Cherokee, not Ojibwe, so it really shouldn't have the Manitou PSP</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I can remove the Pantheon Purview, that's simple enough. And I can replace Wendigo fortunately enough, since in the background the tribe was originally said to be patroned by the spirit Sasquatch. If it's really offensive, I could just declare this a Werewolf AU with the Croatoan tribe still around instead of the Wendigo. That'd have less unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagnusDomine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Just as a heads-up, even with you meaning Dev\u00e1 and not Yazata, I would recommend to be careful around labels like &quot;idiots&quot;. The Yazata are not some quaint fantasy religion once worshipped in the past, their worshippers still exist and are persecuted in multiple states for our continued worship.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Others have already made this point, and revisions will be made in the final version. I apologize for treating the deities of a religion as being less than they are, I let the storytelling side of my brain get ahead of my empathy. I will note however that I try to at least capture some of the feel/perspective of the Tribe for the Totem I'm writing about for their descriptions, and that includes the Get's... less-than-stellar PR side. Are the Yazata idiots? No. Could there be a section of the Get that doesn't like them, or has prejudicial views of them? There certainly was in the past, see the &quot;Swords of Heimdall&quot; if you're interested. For the pantheon's &quot;Relationships&quot; section, I could even note how &quot;Despite claims of idiotic prejudice from, of all things, <i>the Get of Fenris</i>, the Yazata are far more adept at seeing things as they are than some and are offended at the very notion. Relations between them and the rest of the Garou Pantheon have thus been historically less-than-cordial, and they're not the last pantheon to think so of the werewolves.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I\u2019ll be honest: the usage of Wendigo and Uktena as patrons, does disturb me and this attitude applies to the source material as well. This is a prime excuse to change the names, and remove the offensive stereotyping of Native people tied to that, I\u2019m sure they\u2019ll still work fine if you change those two names \ud83d\ude03. And yeah I\u2019m with Manus and Samudra, presenting the gods of real life religions, ones that have historically and presently oppression, as idiots is objectionable on basic principles.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Uktena also had another patron once, but that was called &quot;Skyhawk&quot; and I have no clue what that relates to, so if anyone has any more info that would be helpful. For the stereotyping, I can at least make some changes for the soon-to-not-be-Wendigo tribe, because I'm familiar with some of the Native Culture of my area, though that would replace the &quot;Angry Indian&quot; stereotype with just a ton of fishing... which would probably still be better, I'll admit. I have no clue what to do for Uktena, I've never lived in those areas, so I never picked up any legends or culture via osmosis. If you guys have any information, that would be helpful.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T14:00:49-07:00","id":1405197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405105#post1405105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember: If all they have in common is a name, sometimes you can get away with going &quot;Also, they're not related to [Other figure] and are very tired with the mix-ups.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenris the totem and Fenris the titan have more in common than just a name. both are giant wolves, both are native to Scandinavia, they both dislike the asier, both are cunning but prefer to use strength. and in the wta end times scenario where the get fall to the wyrm Fenris the totem is chained but eventually breaks free and eats existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T15:37:55-07:00","id":1405207,"title":"","content":"I mean like, part of the problem of &quot;Well but there's explicit connections in the Werewolf material&quot; is... Like, I admit I don't know a lot about Werewolf but from what I know of it from this thread, it's not great in terms of sensitivity. With all due respect to the writers of the time, I'm sure they thought they were doing their best but the results will be a mine field to bring into a game with the actual myth it was copied from.<br /> <br /> Like Totem Fenris and Aesir Fenris. How much do they have in common? How similar will they be at your table? Given that, to be blunt, it sounds like the writers of Werewolf looked at Mythic Fenris and went &quot;Copy and paste!&quot; as Wopsie has noted.<br /> <br /> And ultimately you can just go full-on &quot;This is a separate universe not set in the World of Scion&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T16:16:48-07:00","id":1405212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405207#post1405207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean like, part of the problem of &quot;Well but there's explicit connections in the Werewolf material&quot; is... Like, I admit I don't know a lot about Werewolf but from what I know of it from this thread, it's not great in terms of sensitivity. With all due respect to the writers of the time, I'm sure they thought they were doing their best but the results will be a mine field to bring into a game with the actual myth it was copied from.<br /> <br /> Like Totem Fenris and Aesir Fenris. How much do they have in common? How similar will they be at your table? Given that, to be blunt, it sounds like the writers of Werewolf looked at Mythic Fenris and went &quot;Copy and paste!&quot; as Wopsie has noted.<br /> <br /> And ultimately you can just go full-on &quot;This is a separate universe not set in the World of Scion&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly, my mental fix is either the false Fenris I posted earlier or that there different beings with the same nature, explained away by cosmology. I was just noting the similarities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T16:37:54-07:00","id":1405217,"title":"","content":"Or you can just say that is the myth and it\u2019s true, even if it contradicts the other myths. That\u2019s the way myths work in Scion, Fenrir is free or not, both are true if there is a myth telling it. Are TDD gods, ferries or dead kings? All true, they are gods, their stories are about gods, but at some time the story has changed and it is still true, and latter changed again and still true. The magic of Scion is that, no matter what, it\u2019s true. Is Jesus a hippie that got mad on people exploring his religion? True. Is he one of the many prophets that god send to guide humanity? True. Is he the one and only messiah? True. Is he the only manifestation of God (capital G) in the world? True too. Is he \u201cthe greatest American that ever lived\u201d? NO, bad example, there are limits on what can be true...<br /> <br /> My suggestion is, ignore all the other myths, ignore all the connections to the other myths, even references and gods with same name. You can change the WtA mythology if you like, or can keep it the way it is and adapt it to Scion rules.<br /> <br /> Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too.<br /> Each of the myths, real world myths, exists without thinking about any other myth. They also didn\u2019t care much about what people think about other people back then, prejudice is historical and we are changing it gradually now.<br /> <br /> If you want to use WtA myths on your table, what matter is the people around it, if they like or not and how comfortable they are with the ideas. I am not saying that you can play a game about rape or prejudice being cool and correct (it is definitely wrong and you should talk to a psychologist about it), but no matter what you do, someone will be offended by your choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T16:54:48-07:00","id":1405218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405207#post1405207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean like, part of the problem of &quot;Well but there's explicit connections in the Werewolf material&quot; is... Like, I admit I don't know a lot about Werewolf but from what I know of it from this thread, it's not great in terms of sensitivity. With all due respect to the writers of the time, I'm sure they thought they were doing their best but the results will be a mine field to bring into a game with the actual myth it was copied from.<br /> <br /> Like Totem Fenris and Aesir Fenris. How much do they have in common? How similar will they be at your table? Given that, to be blunt, it sounds like the writers of Werewolf looked at Mythic Fenris and went &quot;Copy and paste!&quot; as Wopsie has noted.<br /> <br /> And ultimately you can just go full-on &quot;This is a separate universe not set in the World of Scion&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of the WoD splats have an ambiguous relationship with the gods al best. The Get of Fenris celebrated the idea that Odin was to be slain by Fenris. The Black Furries openly disdained Athena as a servent of Patriarchy. Werewolves saw themselves as having the duty to keep humanity in check. They proudly told of killing humans to cull the herd. They are Titanspawn, they don't share the standard Titan values, but they are, except for a few tribes, the enemies of the Gods. I could see the Children of Gaia and maybe the Bone Gnawers might be seen as respectable to most gods, even friendly. The Glass Walkers, the Silent Striders, the Stargazers, are probably seen as acceptable neutrals. Since the Tuatha also dislike the Irish, they and the Fianna should get along.<br /> <br /> The Cainite Vampires are the accursed of the gods, the Wraiths are those abandoned by the gods, the Cathayan Vampires are devils in service to the gods. None of these are likely friendly to Scions. The Demons are as much on the outs with the gods as Titans. <br /> <br /> Changelings, Mages, Hunters, and Mummies, are different matters They'd interact with Scions and Pantheons as individuals. Perhaps less so in the case of Changelings and Mummies, and most individual in the case Mages. I could see some Patheons trying to recruit these types as allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T17:32:29-07:00","id":1405221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405217#post1405217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can just say that is the myth and it\u2019s true, even if it contradicts the other myths. That\u2019s the way myths work in Scion, Fenrir is free or not, both are true if there is a myth telling it. Are TDD gods, ferries or dead kings? All true, they are gods, their stories are about gods, but at some time the story has changed and it is still true, and latter changed again and still true. The magic of Scion is that, no matter what, it\u2019s true. Is Jesus a hippie that got mad on people exploring his religion? True. Is he one of the many prophets that god send to guide humanity? True. Is he the one and only messiah? True. Is he the only manifestation of God (capital G) in the world? True too. Is he \u201cthe greatest American that ever lived\u201d? NO, bad example, there are limits on what can be true...<br /> <br /> My suggestion is, ignore all the other myths, ignore all the connections to the other myths, even references and gods with same name. You can change the WtA mythology if you like, or can keep it the way it is and adapt it to Scion rules.<br /> <br /> Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too.<br /> Each of the myths, real world myths, exists without thinking about any other myth. They also didn\u2019t care much about what people think about other people back then, prejudice is historical and we are changing it gradually now.<br /> <br /> If you want to use WtA myths on your table, what matter is the people around it, if they like or not and how comfortable they are with the ideas. I am not saying that you can play a game about rape or prejudice being cool and correct (it is definitely wrong and you should talk to a psychologist about it), but no matter what you do, someone will be offended by your choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>that was what I meant when I said different things with the same nature. and honestly, that was my headcanon the whole time. garm the false Fenris came in a flash of inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T18:32:07-07:00","id":1405225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405217#post1405217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I'm going to put on my snobbery glasses. WtA isn't myth, it's barely a cosmology, and if it contains disrespectful depiction of First Nation peoples' beliefs... Yeah, the OP didn't write those depictions, but if you adapt them as they are, that's <i>repeating</i> and <i>perpetuating</i> them. The original writers of WtA aren't going to break into your house and pull a knife on you if you go &quot;Maybe I shouldn't include this insensitive element&quot;. Like, there's a choice that can be made here, and &quot;Well you didn't ORIGINALLY write this element that's problematic at best and actively racist at worst&quot; is a lazy excuse that perpetuates harmful ideas and attitudes.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't think keeping in elements that get a response of &quot;That's a bit of a YIKES right there&quot; is in fact 'ok too'. Like, don't do that, flat-out. Adjust if you need to, go for the spirit of Werewolf without the baggage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-29-2020, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T19:29:56-07:00","id":1405232,"title":"","content":"I agree on the fact it is not properly a myth, more like a cosmology that is not properly structured to fit all that they needed when they created it. I also agree that the best thing that happened to WoD (the original) was to be finished and replaced by CoD, resetting all the wrong things that were written for the wrong reasons.<br /> <br /> But if they are trying to adapt it, they like it the way it is. If the idea is to just play as one of the totems in the world they have been playing as a werewolf, maybe the best to do is just play the thing as is.<br /> <br /> If I was the one trying to rebuild it in a different way, involving less stereotyping, but it\u2019s not my game and I just want they enjoy their game and have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T20:46:16-07:00","id":1405240,"title":"","content":"Question.<br /> <br /> Wouldnt it be more interesting to research the different &quot;werewolves&quot; from actual myths and mythologies.<br /> You could then create a Denizen template for each &quot;type&quot; of werewolf.<br /> <br /> Then, taking inspiration from WtA, you could say these multiple disparate Denizen form together a cult/society that considers its members born to bring battles to the Titans wherever they may be.<br /> <br /> Aome of these theriantrope denizen get chosen and become scions but most just try to do whatever they can to participate in the fight.<br /> <br /> Or would that stray too far from what you are trying to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T20:55:36-07:00","id":1405243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And ultimately you can just go full-on &quot;This is a separate universe not set in the World of Scion&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Issue with that is the whole point of the project is to create a Garou Pantheon... in Scion. A separate world is okay, but by then what's the point of making the conversion? If I'm going to play with only Werewolves and nothing else, why would I or someone else not just play Werewolf?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion is, ignore all the other myths, ignore all the connections to the other myths, even references and gods with same name. You can change the WtA mythology if you like, or can keep it the way it is and adapt it to Scion rules.<br /> <br /> Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too.<br /> Each of the myths, real world myths, exists without thinking about any other myth. They also didn\u2019t care much about what people think about other people back then, prejudice is historical and we are changing it gradually now.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, prejudice is a big theme in Werewolf:the Apocalypse. While the Garou are technically, <i>technically</i> counting under the label of a prejudiced/oppressed minority, throughout their history they have largely been the oppressors. The Garou hate &quot;the other&quot;, they despise it, and their reasons as to why change from person to person. Without that hatred of everything that isn't them, there wouldn't be the Impergium, the War of Rage, the extermination of the Bunyip, or even the entire existence of the Red Talons tribe. There are of course some exceptions, but they're not the rule. The Garou, as a whole and in individual tribes, are hated in turn by a ton of people, and for good reason. This hatred of each other in the metaplot is why the Garou are on the brink of total failure, because they couldn't get their heads out of their asses fast enough to prevent the world's degradation.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rambling, I just emptied my mind on the subject. As to your earlier point, while removing all other references is possible, I'm worried that it wouldn't be recognizable as Werewolf. Or at least, Werewolf: the <i>Apocalypse.</i> I'm fine with changing the First Nation tribes Totems, or even switching which tribe is dead or not, but removing all connections would mean:<ul><li>Pegasus is literally just a flying horse instead of <i>the</i> Pegasus. Now, granted, the basic story structure that White Wolf made of the myth, a wild mythical creature tamed by a hero aided by a foreign power, who after helping the hero gets castrated, and then gets his revenge by tossing the hero into the ocean, is still serviceable, but it does lose just a touch of flavor. Also, why would the Black Furies be in Greece if they weren't going to have interactions with the Greek Gods? Do they live somewhere else?</li> <li>The Fianna are very, very Irish, and removing them from Ireland would take away the entire basis for their culture, even if it is based on a stereotype.</li> <li>The Silent Striders would not exist in their current form at all. If they can't be expulsed from Egypt because that would involve another pantheon, then how did they become wanderers?</li> <li>Stargazers are no longer Buddhist, even if it was a strange variant of it.</li> </ul>There's obviously a lot of minor details that I skipped over, like Ratatoskr no longer being friendly with the Get, the Bunyip with the mythology of the Australian Aborigines, etc. Point is, by removing all connections, you take away a large portion of each tribe's character. And with enough of that character gone, we no longer have Werewolf: the Apocalypse, we have a generic &quot;spirit&quot; pantheon that just so happens to have werewolves in it. The objective is to convert WtA, not to create an entire pantheon wholesale like it's DnD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T21:39:57-07:00","id":1405244,"title":"","content":"Not to be blunt but maybe if these contradictions are so prominent, conversion just isn't going to work?<br /> <br /> Just saying that Scion has basically been built on the assumption that while the pantheons aren't perfect, we're at least not going to be told that they were all monsters in ways that aren't already in their texts.<br /> <br /> This is kind of a problem if we try to cross it with a cosmology like Werewolf the Apocalypse that quite frankly never really focused on mythological accuracy but insisted on making connections to myths anyway. You can make your own decisions on whether or not that's a problem for Werewolf as a setting, but it definitely becomes a problem when a new fictional cosmology starts making judgments on real world mythologies (many of which are still practiced to this day)<br /> <br /> And yeah, quite frankly, Scion doesn't really need Werewolf the Apocalypse. Werewolves already exist in Scion, in the forms of all the mythologies that already featured them. If you want to play a Werewolf in Scion then play one of them. If you want Werewolf the Apocalypse's totems, then play Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T23:31:05-07:00","id":1405249,"title":"","content":"Or maybe, if someone wants to put their own spin on things, that's okay, too? Or is Scion only played &quot;correctly&quot; if you use only the real-world pantheons, with the recognized deities, following their pre-scripted mantles, and paying close attention to detail so you don't risk offending anyone who knows more than you do about the cultures and faiths involved? In the end, it's a game, not a sociology/theology lesson, and if you are running something that is fun, creative, and non-offensive <i>to your group</i>, how is that badwrongfun? A lot of folks here have a great deal of valuable knowledge about the pantheons of our world (I've learned lots, and the fan-written pantheons have been really great), and if you want to be really accurate, you can be. But if you want to stray, and say the Werewolves have their own versions of Gods, or Artemis isn't a virgin after 2,000+ years, or Hastur the Unspeakable is real - <i>why not?</i> This sometimes strays a little closely to &quot;if you aren't doing it our way, you're doig it wrong&quot;, and that's not exactly inviting to an open community and new ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T00:14:40-07:00","id":1405253,"title":"","content":"I mean yeah, ultimately you run whatever game you want, and make up whatever new stuff you want as well.<br /> <br /> I think the issue is more that Scion isn't just a game about fictional entities, its a game that involves real cultural practices. You can do whatever you want with your own games, but saying stuff that's actively wrong about someone else's culture and expecting no push-back or criticism because it's just a game is another matter.<br /> <br /> A lot of it depends on context. Like saying Athena's a tool of the Patriarchy's one thing or that Fenris is unfairly imprisoned by the Aesir is one thing. People from the time and Historians might disagree with you, but the Theoi and Aesir aren't widely followed in the modern day aside from fairly modern pagan revivals. But going around claiming the Yazata or the Deva (both of whom have active faiths around them that have experiences with persecution and colonization) are violent fanatics starts to get iffy. This is even more extreme when you get to actively appropriating figures from First Nations myths like Wendigo and Uktena.<br /> <br /> Like by all means make new stuff, it's messing around with old stuff where things become a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T00:54:38-07:00","id":1405257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405243#post1405243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the rambling, I just emptied my mind on the subject. As to your earlier point, while removing all other references is possible, I'm worried that it wouldn't be recognizable as Werewolf. Or at least, Werewolf: the <i>Apocalypse.</i> I'm fine with changing the First Nation tribes Totems, or even switching which tribe is dead or not, but removing all connections would mean:<ul><li>Pegasus is literally just a flying horse instead of <i>the</i> Pegasus. Now, granted, the basic story structure that White Wolf made of the myth, a wild mythical creature tamed by a hero aided by a foreign power, who after helping the hero gets castrated, and then gets his revenge by tossing the hero into the ocean, is still serviceable, but it does lose just a touch of flavor. Also, why would the Black Furies be in Greece if they weren't going to have interactions with the Greek Gods? Do they live somewhere else?</li> <li>The Fianna are very, very Irish, and removing them from Ireland would take away the entire basis for their culture, even if it is based on a stereotype.</li> <li>The Silent Striders would not exist in their current form at all. If they can't be expulsed from Egypt because that would involve another pantheon, then how did they become wanderers?</li> <li>Stargazers are no longer Buddhist, even if it was a strange variant of it.</li> </ul>There's obviously a lot of minor details that I skipped over, like Ratatoskr no longer being friendly with the Get, the Bunyip with the mythology of the Australian Aborigines, etc. Point is, by removing all connections, you take away a large portion of each tribe's character. And with enough of that character gone, we no longer have Werewolf: the Apocalypse, we have a generic &quot;spirit&quot; pantheon that just so happens to have werewolves in it. The objective is to convert WtA, not to create an entire pantheon wholesale like it's DnD.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is not \u201cremove all connections\u201d, my idea is ignore the other side of the connections. Pegasus is not going to be a different being, and Fianna will still interact with the fairy, what you have to do is consider what is written for WtA as the true and don\u2019t try to explain how it interact with the Theoi, Aesir and TDD. Ignore the connection, not the creature.<br /> <br /> Also, on prejudice, I know WtA deals a lot with prejudice. It is not the main theme, but it\u2019s behind most of the actions of the groups around. What I think is a problem is if the game is about prejudice and the players think it\u2019s ok to have prejudice against real people.<br /> You don\u2019t need to change your game because people in this forum don\u2019t like it, the same way you don\u2019t need to keep it the way it was written because the writers will be angry. That your table, if you want to play Scion using WtA totems, this is a game about playing a god, no matter if people believed in it or not, so this is a good game to use. People in this forum tend to think Scion is a better game because it is about real world myths and the writers did a good research on real life myths, but it\u2019s just a game, and you play as you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:21:02-07:00","id":1405258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405249#post1405249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and if you are running something that is fun, creative, and non-offensive <i>to your group</i>, how is that badwrongfun?</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I were, hypothetically, running a game that featured 110% objectively racist and offensive takes using ethnic stereotypes and dropping slurs but nobody in my game is insulted because they're all white, then that's fine?<br /> <br /> No, fuck that noise. Offensive stereotypical takes aren't okay because you're using them for a select audience, it just means you're using them to an audience that doesn't care about showing some basic goddamn respect.<br /> <br /> It's not being the Fun Police to go &quot;Yo bruh you're borrowing from some hella racist insensitive takes, may want to clean those up a little&quot;. I'm fine with adjusting things for the table but there's lines in everything, and if your response to someone going &quot;This is actually really insensitive from the cultures that the original writers stole this idea from without consulting the cultures and is basically in name only&quot; is &quot;Well that's a big fat cup of not my problem&quot; then I'm sorry but you're an asshole and I will ignore my own signature and say <i>you are in fact doing several things wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> Doing something potentially insensitive by accident? Whatever, it happens, and I'm not holding someone legitimately not realizing against them. Fuck knows I've done some shitty things in the past. But if your response to someone informing you of the shitty thing you accidentally did is &quot;Fuck you I'm sticking to this&quot; then yeah, I'm totally going to call that out.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, 'It's just a game' is <b>not</b> an excuse for knowingly repeating and indulging in REALLY bad stereotyping. And I can't believe I have to explain this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-30-2020, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:23:02-07:00","id":1405259,"title":"","content":"Scion may be a game, but it\u2019s game that deals with real things: cultures and religions, things don\u2019t exist in a vacuum, Wendigo is an actual term from an actual people who actually exist in actual real life, and not only that but they\u2019re an actual people who have actually been repeatedly oppressed both in the past and today. Taking that term, ripping it from it\u2019s context in order to profit off of stereotypes of those real people is legitimately bad on Werewolf: The Apocalypse\u2019s part, and any fan-project should recognize what parts of the source material should stay and what should leave, and racist elements and offensive stereotypes are one of the most important things to remove.<br /> <br /> Edit: also I\u2019m just gonna say this: there is no excuse to knowingly parroting racist elements in a work, like that is not ever ok","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 07-30-2020, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:16:07-07:00","id":1405273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405249#post1405249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe, if someone wants to put their own spin on things, that's okay, too? Or is Scion only played &quot;correctly&quot; if you use only the real-world pantheons, with the recognized deities, following their pre-scripted mantles, and paying close attention to detail so you don't risk offending anyone who knows more than you do about the cultures and faiths involved? In the end, it's a game, not a sociology/theology lesson, and if you are running something that is fun, creative, and non-offensive <i>to your group</i>, how is that badwrongfun? A lot of folks here have a great deal of valuable knowledge about the pantheons of our world (I've learned lots, and the fan-written pantheons have been really great), and if you want to be really accurate, you can be. But if you want to stray, and say the Werewolves have their own versions of Gods, or Artemis isn't a virgin after 2,000+ years, or Hastur the Unspeakable is real - <i>why not?</i> This sometimes strays a little closely to &quot;if you aren't doing it our way, you're doig it wrong&quot;, and that's not exactly inviting to an open community and new ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> here. Being willfully racist in private for fun is no better and has no less negative impact on the world than being racist in public. Your group is never closed off, your game is never just a game, your obligation to be a good, civil person does not end once you sit down at the game table. You and your players leave that table at some point and return to the world at large, and if you do that with vile racist stereotypes, with the idea that offending marginalised people is okay as long as it's fun cemented in your heads, then yes, the fun you had in that game was &quot;badwrong&quot; and will have consequences for everyone you interact with.<br /> <br /> The examples you give are actually good, they skirt around the issues Kyman, Magicjohnny and others have raised (inadvertently, I think, because I know you mean well), but they show where the line is to be drawn. And that is an important line, one that needs to be <i>hard</i>. Involving fictional deities like ones for Werewolves? Not a problem at all, and not something anyone here meant to criticise as such. Involving Hastur? Okay, as long as one is careful to avoid the very racism Lovecraft's work is steeped in. Letting Artemis have sex? That can be a great idea, if you don't veer into misogyny and rape fantasies and instead use it to play upon how all the Greek virgin goddesses are really just expressions of misogyny and rape fantasies the Greeks themselves held. None of this touches upon real-life marginalised groups, none of this offends (to my knowledge) living religions. None of this is what the criticisms in this thread were about. But perpetuating stereotypical, denigerating, harmful depictions of groups that have suffered from these attitudes both historically and in current politics, appropriating elements these groups have asked not to be used by outsiders? That is just racism and contempt plain and simple, and it doesn't matter whether it happens in a game or in the street, it stays just that. And that is where we need to draw the line.<br /> <br /> But I think no one here meant to tear Critian Caceorte down for their ideas. Still racism, cultural appropriation, etc. can happen unknowingly, and they are just as harmful then as if perpetrated willfully. And in such situations it is good, even necessary, that someone taps you on the shoulder and puts what you're doing in perspective, tells you about the larger-scale implications it has that you weren't aware of. And that is what I think people here were trying to do. At least it's what I'm trying to do. And that is not policing other people's games, that's just working towards a civil and open society in which we try to wrangle racism and other divisive forces down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:17:26-07:00","id":1405274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405217#post1405217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not ok.... Abso-fucking-lutely NOT OK to Hel Naraka and Tartarus. It is *never* ok to parrot stupid racist shit... unknowingly parroting racist shit is the fucking bedrock of racism, and going 'someone else said it first so it's ok if you do, is being willfully ignorant at best and morally repugnant at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:36:27-07:00","id":1405277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405249#post1405249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is Scion only played &quot;correctly&quot; if you use only the real-world pantheons, with the recognized deities, following their pre-scripted mantles, and paying close attention to detail so you don't risk offending anyone who knows more than you do about the cultures and faiths involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's played correctly when you don't risk offending real, marginalized, groups that are still suffering; please do not try and frame concern about racism as intellectual elitism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405249#post1405249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, it's a game, not a sociology/theology lesson, and if you are running something that is fun, creative, and non-offensive <i>to your group</i>, how is that badwrongfun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a game excuses nothing, and this is about as useful an argument as 'don't make this political'... just as all debates and opinions are inherently an expression of politics, all interactions are lessons, whether you want to be or not... human beings always learn from each other, and if your game is teaching the table that this is ok, then it is, indeed, 'badwrongfun' because those people aren't going to stay at the table forever, and they're going to take those lessons you taught with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:39:10-07:00","id":1405278,"title":"","content":"I would just like to note also, btw, that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26317\" data-vbnamecard=\"26317\">Critian Caceorte</a> has already said that they're considering ways to change the Native American Tribes, and I whole-heartedly approve of that decision <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My criticism is of the views expressed post that, not of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:53:11-07:00","id":1405281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405217#post1405217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writers had prejudice on native American mythology and general population? Yes, but not your fault. Want to correct it? Ok. Want to use it the way it was wrote? Ok, too. Each of the myths, real world myths, exists without thinking about any other myth. They also didn\u2019t care much about what people think about other people back then, prejudice is historical and we are changing it gradually now.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a fictional game world, you can use mythology however you like it. A great number of World of Darkness supplements come from the perspective of inverting or twisting myths. Demon: The Fallen and Vampire: The Masquerade take a decidedly anti-Christian view of the Judaeo-Christian God. Likewise so did the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina. You're correct that there's nothing wrong with making Zeus a complete monster similar to Kronos unworthy of worship or otherwise inverting and playing around with other mythologies.<br /> <br /> One of my all time favorite books is American Gods and its depiction of Odin is a right asshole.<br /> <br /> However, one should note that one should do this consciously and as part of storytelling as opposed to doing it because of crappy research or going with the racism of previous writers. I'm a huge fan of Indiana Jones but I would never uncritically ape the Thuggee of the Temple of Doom. Because it was just bad writing and would make any player who knows anything about the real deal annoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:12:34-07:00","id":1405284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405281#post1405281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a fictional game world, you can use mythology however you like it. A great number of World of Darkness supplements come from the perspective of inverting or twisting myths. Demon: The Fallen and Vampire: The Masquerade take a decidedly anti-Christian view of the Judaeo-Christian God. Likewise so did the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina. You're correct that there's nothing wrong with making Zeus a complete monster similar to Kronos unworthy of worship or otherwise inverting and playing around with other mythologies.<br /> <br /> One of my all time favorite books is American Gods and its depiction of Odin is a right asshole.<br /> <br /> However, one should note that one should do this consciously and as part of storytelling as opposed to doing it because of crappy research or going with the racism of previous writers. I'm a huge fan of Indiana Jones but I would never uncritically ape the Thuggee of the Temple of Doom. Because it was just bad writing and would make any player who knows anything about the real deal annoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again I'd reply that there is a great difference between creating a malignant or inaccurate depiction of Greek, Norse, or Christian figures in a society predominantly shaped by those cultures, and doing the same to the representatives of minority cultures. On the inverse, anti-White and anti-Christian prejudice is very real in e.g. Japan or India. I'd be just as outraged about a piece of media from there beating down on the minorities in their own societies. Every group, every player and GM, has a responsibility to <i>not be a dick</i> when dealing with sensitive cultural material. There's a difference between playing with your own heritage and someone else's. The latter requires a lot more work, sensitivity, and readiness to admit and correct mistakes. If that seems too daunting to someone, that's okay. Games <i>should</i> be fun. If someone wants a game that carries none of these responsibilities, they can easily just stick to the less contentious Pantheons like the ones you mentioned, Theoi, Aesir, etc. But once again, &quot;in a fictional game world, you can use mythology however you like it&quot; is only true to a degree - you<i> can</i>, the same way you<i> can</i> be racist and contemptful towards minorities in a myriad other ways, but that doesn't mean that you<i> should</i>, or that it doesn't make you a bad person, or that others are not right to criticise you for it. No game happens in a vacuum, and just because a wrong is happening in a game setting doesn't make it a right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":"I'm not accusing anyone in particular of anything in particular. 07-30-2020, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:27:54-07:00","id":1405288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405281#post1405281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a huge fan of Indiana Jones but I would never uncritically ape the Thuggee of the Temple of Doom. Because it was just bad writing and would make any player who knows anything about the real deal annoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I wouldn't recommend critically aping it either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> About the only good thing I can say about Temple of Doom's Kali is that at least it's not Supernatural's Kali <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:27:54-07:00","id":1405289,"title":"","content":"Yeah there\u2019s a massive difference between an American or European writer presenting Odin or the Christian god as dicks, and perpetuating harmful stereotypes of oppressed minorities. The former doesn\u2019t hurt anyone, Christianity in the West is ridiculously huge, a writer in the West portraying their god in a negative light isn\u2019t going to hurt anyone. Meanwhile the thing about the Thuggees in Indiana Jones is legitimately harmful, as it perpetuates harmful stereotypes. The same applies to WTA and it\u2019s approach towards Native people\u2019s, it perpetuates legitimately harmful stereotypes of Native people as primitive, a stereotype that has a long and ongoing history of delegitimizating Native peoples and their rights. As Sacerdos says, there\u2019s a difference between playing around with your heritage and messing with someone else\u2019s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:44:56-07:00","id":1405293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405284#post1405284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again I'd reply that there is a great difference between creating a malignant or inaccurate depiction of Greek, Norse, or Christian figures in a society predominantly shaped by those cultures, and doing the same to the representatives of minority cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue close to me as I was suspended from school for a week because my Vampire books were decreed to be anti-Christian. My school declared they had ownership of the idea of God and the right to determine how he was presented.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the idea is that there is a ONE TRUE DEPICTION of cosmological figures and myth and that religious figures are beyond reproach. It denies them use in satirical or countermanding narratives that challenge the fundamental assumptions about mythologies. It's the attitude that the Church of Satan should not exist because they are atheists misusing the mythology of Judaeo-Christianity or disrespecting the faith of people like Jesus.<br /> <br /> It also implies ownership of shared cultural heritage that absolutely everyone should own. Far Right believers in Odin and Thor should have no more ownership of them than Marvel comics or someone on the street because they are part of the shared cultural heritage. I'm a believer in Christianity myself but everyone should have the right to satirize the Church, Angels, God, and more if they believe or don't. Dogma, Steve Jackson's In Nomine, DC's Lucifer, and more benefiting society as they challenge assumptions about my faith.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it runs into the fact that shared cultural mythology can and should be something we, the audience, know is used in a medium that we know is fantasy. Wonder Woman's Greek Gods are not the Greek Gods of any actual believers and no one should tell Percy Jackson's writer that he can't use them in a story. Same for Michael Carpenter having supernatural Christian powers in the Dresden Files. Artistic license should be allowed in fiction because it is not affecting the whole.<br /> <br /> Take note that I say that while saying the PURE ONES and the Native American tribal depiction in Werewolf is bullshit because it's badly written dumbassery that is presented as fact rather than satire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the inverse, anti-White and anti-Christian prejudice is very real in e.g. Japan or India. I'd be just as outraged about a piece of media from there beating down on the minorities in their own societies. </div> </div> </div>I should mention that my defense applies to NEON GENESIS EVANGELION, BAYONETTA, and SHIN MEGAMI TENSEI.<br /> <br /> In Bayonetta, you kill angels. You eventually kill God.<br /> <br /> Not my bag but that's the story and it has no effect on my religion.<br /> <br /> I think that there's a pretty large state between, &quot;using the mythology of another society as part of your fictional cosmology&quot; and &quot;actively misrepresents real-life history in order to make said cosmology.&quot; Which is to say the treatment of Native Americans in Werewolf is terrible because its bad history but it's not the same as saying that no one can use anyone else's mythology as researched.<br /> <br /> Victor Lavalle is a black man and he wrote THE BALLAD OF BLACK TOM which is an inversion of the Cthulhu Mythos. H.P. Lovecraft would not have approved. And you know what? Fuck HP Lovecraft. Victor could also write a bunch of books about Odin and Thor getting their ass kicked by his black protagonist and good for him. It has artistic merit as social satire despite the idea he's not &quot;of&quot; Nordic culture.<br /> <br /> Which I suppose all means:<br /> <br /> &quot;I think the problems with Werewolf aren't presenting that the myths of Native Americans differently, it's presenting them as if they were fact in RL.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you are right, punching up is very different from punching down.<br /> <br /> Sorry.<br /> <br /> Complex issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-30-2020, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:00:52-07:00","id":1405295,"title":"","content":"That is an absurdist comparison. Culturally Christian writers in a predominately Christian country using said openly proselytized religion in their fiction, is absolutely NOTHING like people in the position of cultural imperial power rewriting a colonized people\u2019s very private sacred traditions for their own amusement. Don\u2019t scream \u201ccensorship\u201d just because other people have the free speech to call it out as a jerk thing to do.<br /> <br /> There is a reason the Scion writers are applying ethical guidelines in which pantheons get written up and the need for consultants or writers from continuously living traditions to cover them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-30-2020, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:12:01-07:00","id":1405297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405293#post1405293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a statement in criticism of the overarching religious institution of the society you are a part of is light years different from taking the culture of a historically (and presently) oppressed people... they are not the same, and no, you do not just get to use it in your fiction without the permission of the culture you are using... your creative license as an author <i>does not overrule or give you the right to ignore their opinions... if they are unamused by it, it should absolutely be scrapped.</i> I cannot believe that this still needs to be said in the year of your Lord 2020. There is also a great difference between a black man re-purposing Lovecraft and a white person doing so to First Nations myth... as for Riordan, note that he is, in fact, NOT writing about Yoruba or Mayan or Hindu or Ojibwe Mythology, because he is a writer that understands and respects this, so please do not use him in this false argument... and I will not get started on the abomination that is Jim Butcher's use of Navajo myth, <i>because it is a cultural taboo to talk about and I respect that and it should never have been written.</i>.<br /> <br /> To that end, note that the Scion writers also wanted to do a Navajo Pantheon for Demigod but scrapped it because no member of that culture agreed to consult with them... which is the kind of cultural sensitivity I applaud them for and hope they continue to practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-30-2020, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:22:00-07:00","id":1405299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405297#post1405297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making a statement in criticism of the overarching religious institution of the society you are a part of is light years different from taking the culture of a historically (and presently) oppressed people... they are not the same, and no, you do not just get to use it in your fiction without the permission of the culture you are using... your creative license as an author <i>does not overrule or give you the right to ignore their opinions... if they are unamused by it, it should absolutely be scrapped.</i> I cannot believe that this still needs to be said in the year of your Lord 2020. There is also a great difference between a black man re-purposing Lovecraft and a white person doing so to First Nations myth... as for Riordan, note that he is, in fact, NOT writing about Yoruba or Mayan or Hindu or Ojibwe Mythology, because he is a writer that understands and respects this, so please do not use him in this false argument... and I will not get started on the abomination that is Jim Butcher's use of Navajo myth, <i>because it is a cultural taboo to talk about and I respect that and it should never have been written.</i>.<br /> <br /> To that end, note that the Scion writers also wanted to do a Navajo Pantheon for Demigod but scrapped it because no member of that culture agreed to consult with them... which is the kind of cultural sensitivity I applaud them for and hope they continue to practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, hence why I said that there's a large elements of punching up versus down and misrepresentation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-30-2020, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:43:31-07:00","id":1405302,"title":"","content":"No, I am outraged at the first paragraph you had written about nationalism and implying that being sensitive to cultures is akin to using mythology for propaganda, when the actual propaganda was done by the writers appropriating it, not the cultures.<br /> <br /> I am outraged at the idea that anyone here was implying there be one one true depiction, when we were actually arguing against an unfounded depiction by those outside the community the myths belong to.<br /> <br /> I am outraged by the idea that you seem to think that these stories are free fodder for use in satirical narratives to begin with when they are not.<br /> <br /> I am outraged at the idea that you think everyone should have shared ownership of cultures whose members are still treated like absolute shit, and that this is somehow comparable to the use of Christian (and specifically Christian and not Abrahamic since Jewish and Muslim traditions get appropriated and misused all the time) material in media.<br /> <br /> I am outraged that despite earlier points about how fantasy portrayals are just as harmful as supposedly realistic ones, you seem to think that use of these figures in mediums known to be fantasy excuses them, and then invoke the name of an author who has publicly apologized for treating the Theoi as a dead faith and another author who should absolutely be criticized for his portrayals of Native myth.<br /> <br /> I'm outraged that you think &quot;the problems with Werewolf aren't presenting that the myths of Native Americans differently, it's presenting them as if they were fact in RL&quot; when no, the problems are that the portrayal was done badly and without consultation at all, because a thousand disclaimers of 'these aren't real Native Americans' will not change the fact that they are being coded as such.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't think we agree quite as much as you seem to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T04:49:06-07:00","id":1405303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405299#post1405299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, hence why I said that there's a large elements of punching up versus down and misrepresentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still working on my reply to your original long post. Could you please stop editing your posts so much? It makes engaging with your arguments hard (as seen with Samudra, who just replied to a statement that no longer exists) ^^'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:00:03-07:00","id":1405305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405302#post1405302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I am outraged at the first paragraph you had written about nationalism and implying that being sensitive to cultures is akin to using mythology for propaganda, when the actual propaganda was done by the writers appropriating it, not the cultures.<br /> <br /> I am outraged at the idea that anyone here was implying there be one one true depiction, when we were actually arguing against an unfounded depiction by those outside the community the myths belong to.<br /> <br /> I am outraged by the idea that you seem to think that these stories are free fodder for use in satirical narratives to begin with when they are not.<br /> <br /> I am outraged at the idea that you think everyone should have shared ownership of cultures whose members are still treated like absolute shit, and that this is somehow comparable to the use of Christian (and specifically Christian and not Abrahamic since Jewish and Muslim traditions get appropriated and misused all the time) material in media.<br /> <br /> I am outraged that despite earlier points about how fantasy portrayals are just as harmful as supposedly realistic ones, you seem to think that use of these figures in mediums known to be fantasy excuses them, and then invoke the name of an author who has publicly apologized for treating the Theoi as a dead faith and another author who should absolutely be criticized for his portrayals of Native myth.<br /> <br /> I'm outraged that you think &quot;the problems with Werewolf aren't presenting that the myths of Native Americans differently, it's presenting them as if they were fact in RL&quot; when no, the problems are that the portrayal was done badly and without consultation at all, because a thousand disclaimers of 'these aren't real Native Americans' will not change the fact that they are being coded as such.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't think we agree quite as much as you seem to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I agree with all of this. Why I deleted it. It wasn't relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405303#post1405303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still working on my reply to your original long post. Could you please stop editing your posts so much? It makes engaging with your arguments hard (as seen with Samudra, who just replied to a statement that no longer exists) ^^'</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't want to keep something that was incorrect for the argument.<br /> <br /> But yes, the importance of satire and working against ethnostate uses of mythology is something that is very important to me. I grew up in the Deep South and the misuse of and misdepiction of people are things that are very important to me to fight. In the place I was born in, Christianity and misrepresentations were routinely used as weapons against ethnic minorities and attacking these things are important. Bad history like the use of Native Americans as a &quot;everything was peaceful and beautiful and living in the Earth&quot; is almost as harmful. Every culture should be treated respectfully and with deep research to make it better. Hence my Temple of Doom example that is just racist nonsense.<br /> <br /> Part of my worries is the attempt to equate use of fiction with actually protecting minorities, though, which is not. One of this is due to the attacks on Kosoko Jackson.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://reason.com/2019/02/28/he-was-part-of-a-twitter-mob-that-attack/\" target=\"_blank\">https://reason.com/2019/02/28/he-was...b-that-attack/</a><br /> <br /> Comparing fantasy to real life cultures is unintentionally very racist. The attempts to incorporate Native American culture into Werewolf was designed to provide non-white perspective and a rebuttal to heroic American narratives--but it was, of course, badly handled B.S. that made things worse than better. I also note that Werewolf has struggled to remove white nationalist fans over the years.<br /> <br /> I remember the Swords of Heimdall getting killed off because, according to Word of God, people kept showing up with their Get of Fenris Pure Bloods as members at LARPS. Justifying their racism as &quot;playing in character.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-30-2020, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:05:19-07:00","id":1405308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405305#post1405305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. I agree with all of this. Why I deleted it. It wasn't relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, I didn't want to keep something that was incorrect for the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll give up on my reply, then. I'm not good at hitting moving targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T05:11:08-07:00","id":1405313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405308#post1405308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'll give up on my reply, then. I'm not good at hitting moving targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you convinced me.<br /> <br /> I