16"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:36:02-07:00","id":1405442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405431#post1405431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will always support the freedom to use the imagination. It seems to me that you are so into &amp;quot;sensitivity&amp;quot; you'd freely kick any and all basic human rights to the curb. Now I get why hate speech is evil. As a somewhat fem bisexual working class man from West Virginia trust me I've been the target of plenty of hate speech. Being a white guy with an education I've certainly been told I am the oppressor (by a Wealthy Hispanic Woman from a family that has been wealthy since the King of Spain granted them lands in New Mexico no less, I didn't bow when we met, I kid you not, she was old money to the max). I've plenty of experience of being bullied by college kids with &amp;quot;sensitivity&amp;quot; quick to gang up on a working class guy with Asperger's. (Side note, I am on the Left, if I were European I'd be voting socialist). <br /> So I find people demanding vast restrictions on free speach because of &amp;quot;sensitivity'&amp;quot; suspicious at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you seriously just accuse someone of wanting to trample on human rights just because they\u2019re rightfully offending by offensive material? Isn\u2019t that literally breaking the \u201cno personal attacks rule\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:37:56-07:00","id":1405444,"title":"","content":"Charles, listen astromancer here is being very insensitive abd rude. I think you should ban him from.this thread,i don't want a lenghty discussion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T19:35:07-07:00","id":1405452,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I figured it would be good to do a warning first. To be aware that at the end of the day we're discussing the magical world of make believe's handling of RL religion.<br /> <br /> If it turns into RL insults after this points or accusations of evil then they can leave the thread or I'll shut it down.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there are some personal attacks here and rules broken but I'm being somewhat more lenient than I should be here.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-30-2020, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T23:50:26-07:00","id":1405482,"title":"","content":"I haven't left the thread, but work comes before posting. I plan to have a more in-depth rebuttal of some of the points made above, but at this point, I just want to state that 1) I'm not trying to personally attack anyone, 2) I am not oblivious to cultural issues (in Canada we have our own ugly history with the First Nations), and 3) i strongly disagree wih Samudra's assertion that, in essence, I have an obligation to maintain complete and faithful adherence to any and all cultures and beliefs not my own, even if any variations take place only within my own group, at my own table. I'm not a bigot, or oblivious to diffrent cultures, but if I choose to stray from the stories, or play a pantheon without fully studying everything first, it isn't your place to tell me I can't.<br /> On another point - Rick Riordan did a series after Percy Jackson. It involved the Egyptian Gods. Are people of the opinion that this was something he shouldn't have done? Where do we draw the line? If I play an RPG based in a large multicultural city (such as Vancouver or Toronto), am I, as a white man, being inappropriate if I include non-stereotyped (but still not exhaustively-researched) npcs of Asian, Arabic, Black, Indo-Canadian, or other non-white backgrounds? And if I don't include them, isn't that whitewashing? Similarly, if Scion includes multiple non-Western pantheons, am I wrong to want to use them, change the course of the myths, and put my own spin on it?<br /> This is a very complex subject indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:15:48-07:00","id":1405483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405444#post1405444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charles, listen astromancer here is being very insensitive abd rude. I think you should ban him from.this thread,i don't want a lenghty discussion</div> </div> </div> </div>Come on sir that is not how banning works, you can't order a Moderator to ban someone and also say you don't have to justify yourself or discuss the ban. The Scion forum has a bad reputation for gatekeeping as it is. And mods before have been tapped on the shoulder by their friends to step in as personal favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:19:40-07:00","id":1405485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405442#post1405442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you seriously just accuse someone of wanting to trample on human rights just because they\u2019re rightfully offending by offensive material? Isn\u2019t that literally breaking the \u201cno personal attacks rule\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an uncharitable reading, and it is insulting you are accusing someone of personal attacks. I find your smears more definable as violating the &quot;no personal attacks rule&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:25:08-07:00","id":1405487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405225#post1405225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay I'm going to put on my snobbery glasses. WtA isn't myth, it's barely a cosmology, and if it contains disrespectful depiction of First Nation peoples' beliefs... Yeah, the OP didn't write those depictions, but if you adapt them as they are, that's <i>repeating</i> and <i>perpetuating</i> them. The original writers of WtA aren't going to break into your house and pull a knife on you if you go &quot;Maybe I shouldn't include this insensitive element&quot;. Like, there's a choice that can be made here, and &quot;Well you didn't ORIGINALLY write this element that's problematic at best and actively racist at worst&quot; is a lazy excuse that perpetuates harmful ideas and attitudes.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't think keeping in elements that get a response of &quot;That's a bit of a YIKES right there&quot; is in fact 'ok too'. Like, don't do that, flat-out. Adjust if you need to, go for the spirit of Werewolf without the baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just said you weren't very familiar with Werewolf the Apocalypse. By the time it reached Revised era I saw no problem with depictions. Use specific examples when trying to cancel an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:25:54-07:00","id":1405488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405485#post1405485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an uncharitable reading, and it is insulting you are accusing someone of personal attacks. I find your smears more definable as violating the &quot;no personal attacks rule&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally, <i>literally</i> what Astromancer said there. &quot;You'd freely kick any and all basic human rights to the curb&quot;. Any and all of them. How can that be read charitably? And if accusing someone of personal attacks is insulting (and thus, by implication, shouldn't be done, even though personal attacks are against the rules and <i>should</i> be investigated), then why are you doing it yourself? What is calling Magicjohnny no more than paraphrasing what Astromancer said &quot;smears&quot; if not insulting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:27:34-07:00","id":1405489,"title":"","content":"Tell me how else am I supposed to read:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405431#post1405431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to me that you are so into &amp;quot;sensitivity&amp;quot; you'd freely kick any and all basic human rights to the curb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I\u2019m genuinely asking, how can this be anything other then a personal attack towards Samudra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:29:37-07:00","id":1405490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405482#post1405482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't left the thread, but work comes before posting. I plan to have a more in-depth rebuttal of some of the points made above, but at this point, I just want to state that 1) I'm not trying to personally attack anyone, 2) I am not oblivious to cultural issues (in Canada we have our own ugly history with the First Nations), and 3) i strongly disagree wih Samudra's assertion that, in essence, I have an obligation to maintain complete and faithful adherence to any and all cultures and beliefs not my own, even if any variations take place only within my own group, at my own table. I'm not a bigot, or oblivious to diffrent cultures, but if I choose to stray from the stories, or play a pantheon without fully studying everything first, it isn't your place to tell me I can't.<br /> On another point - Rick Riordan did a series after Percy Jackson. It involved the Egyptian Gods. Are people of the opinion that this was something he shouldn't have done? Where do we draw the line? If I play an RPG based in a large multicultural city (such as Vancouver or Toronto), am I, as a white man, being inappropriate if I include non-stereotyped (but still not exhaustively-researched) npcs of Asian, Arabic, Black, Indo-Canadian, or other non-white backgrounds? And if I don't include them, isn't that whitewashing? Similarly, if Scion includes multiple non-Western pantheons, am I wrong to want to use them, change the course of the myths, and put my own spin on it?<br /> This is a very complex subject indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody has said you can\u2019t use non-white mythologies or that you have to be educated in them, all people have been have been saying is that you should be respectful in your portrayals of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:36:48-07:00","id":1405491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405259#post1405259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion may be a game, but it\u2019s game that deals with real things: cultures and religions, things don\u2019t exist in a vacuum, Wendigo is an actual term from an actual people who actually exist in actual real life, and not only that but they\u2019re an actual people who have actually been repeatedly oppressed both in the past and today. Taking that term, ripping it from it\u2019s context in order to profit off of stereotypes of those real people is legitimately bad on Werewolf: The Apocalypse\u2019s part, and any fan-project should recognize what parts of the source material should stay and what should leave, and racist elements and offensive stereotypes are one of the most important things to remove.<br /> <br /> Edit: also I\u2019m just gonna say this: there is no excuse to knowingly parroting racist elements in a work, like that is not ever ok</div> </div> </div> </div>You know many MANY would consider the basic idea of the game sacrilegious right? Like how is the depiction of Wendigo less sacrilegious in Scion? How is it not sacrilegious to shoehorn all mighty mythological figures into the Greek Framework of God and Titan, as well as Primordial. Point out specifics that you don't want from Werewolf. Werewolf is a game where human history and myth are inaccurate lenses of a shadow history of the world through human lenses. If someone wants to do a Scion game in the Werewolf Setting then they are assuming a game setting different then the standard and you can't threadcrap just because you don't like their idea for a game. Scion is a fictitious game that draws upon myths and legends in their world building and themes, but it is a game, and it doesn't help the gameline to gatekeep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:42:00-07:00","id":1405493,"title":"","content":"Respecting real life cultures and their faiths isn\u2019t gatekeeping, if anything it\u2019s the opposite it allows members of those cultures and faiths to feel safe, to feel that the community does indeed care. The problem with Werewolf and it\u2019s treatment of Native people, is that it perpetuates stereotypes of Native people as violent and savage and animalistic and primitive, stereotypes that are used in real life to hurt those people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:43:13-07:00","id":1405494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405487#post1405487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just said you weren't very familiar with Werewolf the Apocalypse. By the time it reached Revised era I saw no problem with depictions. Use specific examples when trying to cancel an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay you want something a bit more specific?<br /> <br /> Maybe don't use a Patron literally called Wendigo. Because it doesn't take MUCH research to learn that the wendigo is a very serious monster to the culture that these stories come from, and is probably not something you would make anything other than a terrible antagonist, at best a tragic one. Oh look at that, I did a bit of research despite not being from any of the First Nations. If you want to keep the patron, change the name and completely divorce them from the concept. Or remove the patron entirely. It's basic manners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do we draw the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as you note, it's a complicated subject, there is no SINGULAR line. That kind of &quot;Where's the line?&quot; rhetoric is usually a smokescreen used by insincere people to try and obfuscate when they're being insensitive assholes. Broad universal statements aren't going to apply because much of this comes down to context.<br /> <br /> But you want a line? Here's a line: If a cultural group has gone out and said &quot;You got this all wrong and we would prefer you stop this&quot; <b>you fucking stop that</b>. This isn't rocket surgery, it's basic respect. And you definitely don't keep repeating the stuff that they spoke up against, and when someone points out that hey this is kind of Not Cool, you don't shrug and go &quot;Well that's how it was done in the past&quot;. That's never an acceptable excuse.<br /> <br /> Variations happen. You can play a bit within reason. Take some spins. But some things are going too far. I'm not going to write a story where Brahma beats Sarasvati. I'm not going to run a game where I say that Indra, Zeus, and Horus are the same God in different hats. I'm not going to run a game where Cortez is a Scion of Quetzacoatl and implicitly blessing the Spanish invasion of the Americas.<br /> <br /> You know, basic decency. Basic manners. Basic respect. I'm sorry if that's too much of an ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:46:31-07:00","id":1405496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405482#post1405482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't left the thread, but work comes before posting. I plan to have a more in-depth rebuttal of some of the points made above, but at this point, I just want to state that 1) I'm not trying to personally attack anyone, 2) I am not oblivious to cultural issues (in Canada we have our own ugly history with the First Nations), and 3) i strongly disagree wih Samudra's assertion that, in essence, I have an obligation to maintain complete and faithful adherence to any and all cultures and beliefs not my own, even if any variations take place only within my own group, at my own table. I'm not a bigot, or oblivious to diffrent cultures, but if I choose to stray from the stories, or play a pantheon without fully studying everything first, it isn't your place to tell me I can't.<br /> On another point - Rick Riordan did a series after Percy Jackson. It involved the Egyptian Gods. Are people of the opinion that this was something he shouldn't have done? Where do we draw the line? If I play an RPG based in a large multicultural city (such as Vancouver or Toronto), am I, as a white man, being inappropriate if I include non-stereotyped (but still not exhaustively-researched) npcs of Asian, Arabic, Black, Indo-Canadian, or other non-white backgrounds? And if I don't include them, isn't that whitewashing? Similarly, if Scion includes multiple non-Western pantheons, am I wrong to want to use them, change the course of the myths, and put my own spin on it?<br /> This is a very complex subject indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only repeat that no group is ever isolated and there will never be anything that happens at your table that will not have &quot;real life&quot; repercussions. You and your players are not magically excluded from society and its weave for the duration of your game session. And you're right, it is not Samudra's place to tell you what you can and can't do. It is, however, absolutely his place to tell you you are behaving badly, insultingly, egregiously if you butcher a religion that is sacred to him and people he cares about for a personal idea of &quot;fun.&quot; In general, there's a law of proportion - the more important a Pantheon or, to use your example, the ethnic background of a character is, the more research should advisably go into that. If your plot hinges upon an idea from a specific religion, I'd consider it common decency to look up if you're portraying that idea respectfully, or at least to address and improve your mistakes if you only realise them later. And that's what this is really about. Not free speech, not policing people's private lives, it's us saying &quot;Yeah, you <i>can </i>do this, but we will consider you a dick if you do.&quot; Same for those NPCs. It's good if your Desi character is not a delivery guy with a funny accent, and if they make a one-time appearance, that's probably enough. If they are integral to the plot, it bears fleshing them out with some real-world experience instead of just your fantasies. And I think none of this is asking too much; like I said, if it is, if you simply don't have the time or resources for that kind of research, that is totally okay, and there are a number of Pantheons that will not cause you conscience issues using &quot;blindly.&quot; I have sorted out the examples people gave on that previously.<br /> <br /> Two points I still want to address. One is that everyone here touts Rick Riordan as the patron saint of doing what you will with mythology, when he is really quite the opposite. This is a man who consciously stuck to mythologies that are considered part of the &quot;Western&quot; heritage to various degrees and opened a whole imprint of its own so authors who were <i>actually</i> from non-White cultures could have a platform to write books about their mythologies themselves. This is a man who has repeatedly apologised for what mistakes he made and has sought to improve in later books. He even apologised for parts of his books being found disrespectful by Hellenic revivalists, which is a plain rebuttal to the earlier example of him not being obligated by an &quot;authority&quot; or &quot;ownership&quot; on Greek religion. So really, to all the people who have used him as an example here: You are misrepresenting this man. He is not the idol of your artistic license on other people's heritage, he is the respectful and circumspect creator we are <i>asking </i>you to be.<br /> Lastly, there is the repeated line of &quot;This is a very complex subject,&quot; which says very little and only makes me think that people want the discussion to end as &quot;too complex,&quot; as impossible to find a solution. While there are, indeed, intricate complexities at play here, those can be resolved through debate and reasoning (the stuff we're doing here) and most of all by listening to the people affected (the stuff people accusing Samudra of human rights violations have not been doing). And at the core of it all are quite simple questions of respect and contempt, of right and wrong, and I really don't think we should try to muddle <i>those</i> up as somehow grey and impossible to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":".  Fixed some spelling 07-31-2020, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:48:53-07:00","id":1405498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405488#post1405488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is literally, <i>literally</i> what Astromancer said there. &quot;You'd freely kick any and all basic human rights to the curb&quot;. Any and all of them. How can that be read charitably? And if accusing someone of personal attacks is insulting (and thus, by implication, shouldn't be done, even though personal attacks are against the rules and <i>should</i> be investigated), then why are you doing it yourself? What is calling Magicjohnny no more than paraphrasing what Astromancer said &quot;smears&quot; if not insulting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people here constantly bully others who dare to disagree with them here. I am pointing out the fallacy in the logic here. And if you guys don't get CTPhips you will try to go over his head and get Mods that agree with you to contradict him. The rules are simple don't thread crap. If you don't like the idea of this thread then don't thread crap just don't interact with it. You are insulting and mudslinging someone, and when someone points it out you accuse that person of breaking the rules. This is why ideally we have mod arbitration, because you can't just dogpile on someone you disagree with. If you don't like the basic premise of this thread you are not allowed to dogpile it. He says you would freely kick human rights to the curb because in his opinion you would. You can't selectively just declare your insults as not insulting because its true, but who you are disagreeing with is &quot;objectively wrong&quot; so they are insulting. How is this not gatekeeping? If the logic here is Werewolf is wrong, then why aren't you trying to cancel it? By the time we reach revised and W20 they fixed things, there is rich lore, and if someone wants to do a game like that its their right. You can't try to ban people because they disagree with you. You can't ban Astromancer when he is actually engaging with the original poster of the thread and you guys are engaging negatively with the very premise of the thread. This happens all the time here and it is not right. People here bully people for not being minorities but then turn around and bully minorities for not agreeing with them, that is inappropriate. Doing a Manitou Pantheon is just as sacrilegious as other games touching upon the same topics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:51:13-07:00","id":1405499,"title":"","content":"Yeah I\u2019m friends with a hindu who loves Percy Jackson and they have repeatedly praised Rick for actually trying to be respectful and for apologizing when he does wrong things unknowingly, he isn\u2019t some pinnacle of artistic license of heritage, he\u2019s a dude who recognizes that artistic license isn\u2019t an excuse for perpetuating harmful ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:53:33-07:00","id":1405501,"title":"","content":"Nobody here as far as I\u2019m aware has bullied people for not being minorities, the only thing we have been doing is just saying that maybe just maybe perpetuating harmful stereotypes of real life people is bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T01:07:17-07:00","id":1405503,"title":"","content":"Also it should be noted that the Manitou pantheon was written with the help of members of the Algonquin people, and the writer is himself a Native, Lakota specifically and friends with members of the Algonquin who he called upon to help with the project. So it\u2019s not really disrespectful, because it was made with the help and assistance of the people the topic is important to. It also helps a lot that it doesn\u2019t perpetuate harmful stereotypes of Native peoples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T01:12:05-07:00","id":1405504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405494#post1405494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay you want something a bit more specific?<br /> <br /> Maybe don't use a Patron literally called Wendigo. Because it doesn't take MUCH research to learn that the wendigo is a very serious monster to the culture that these stories come from, and is probably not something you would make anything other than a terrible antagonist, at best a tragic one. Oh look at that, I did a bit of research despite not being from any of the First Nations. If you want to keep the patron, change the name and completely divorce them from the concept. Or remove the patron entirely. It's basic manners.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because, as you note, it's a complicated subject, there is no SINGULAR line. That kind of &quot;Where's the line?&quot; rhetoric is usually a smokescreen used by insincere people to try and obfuscate when they're being insensitive assholes. Broad universal statements aren't going to apply because much of this comes down to context.<br /> <br /> But you want a line? Here's a line: If a cultural group has gone out and said &quot;You got this all wrong and we would prefer you stop this&quot; <b>you fucking stop that</b>. This isn't rocket surgery, it's basic respect. And you definitely don't keep repeating the stuff that they spoke up against, and when someone points out that hey this is kind of Not Cool, you don't shrug and go &quot;Well that's how it was done in the past&quot;. That's never an acceptable excuse.<br /> <br /> Variations happen. You can play a bit within reason. Take some spins. But some things are going too far. I'm not going to write a story where Brahma beats Sarasvati. I'm not going to run a game where I say that Indra, Zeus, and Horus are the same God in different hats. I'm not going to run a game where Cortez is a Scion of Quetzacoatl and implicitly blessing the Spanish invasion of the Americas.<br /> <br /> You know, basic decency. Basic manners. Basic respect. I'm sorry if that's too much of an ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read the gameline you would understand they address things from the outside the human perspective and subverts the expectations. Werewolf is a game where you play sacred Monsters. Hence why Fenris a godbeast of the Apocalypse is shown from the perspective of Fenris, pointing out what if the legend was inaccurate because they didn't know the point of view of Fenris, who even in the stories is a character of tragedy, he was judged and sentenced without committing a crime, only because he was a fierce potential threat. Wendigo is a sacred monster as well, it was a spirit that scourges mankind for the taboo of cannibalism, because in the North Cannibalism was a serious threat when people run out of food and thus it was important to have stories to condemn it. In Werewolf the original totem was Sasquatch, and in the Lore of the game the crossing of the great strait to the Americas changed that aspect of Sasquatch into Wendigo, they serve a crucial role in punishing taboos and being sacred monsters, but they also walk a fine line because eating human flesh is against the Litany and its hinted at that maybe Wendigo will fall or maybe Wendigo won't fall, but there are corrupt Wendigo spirits and non corrupt ones. It is like the Devil Tigers Dharma there are Devils that discourage people from the path of inequity by tempting others and those who fall for temptation are punished as an example. World of Darkness is not black and white it is gray, and you do a disservice to crap on games when you aren't a fan of them and haven't read their books but make erroneous assumptions and judge others based on these assumptions. And it would be simpler to be humble and try apologizing rather then double down and try to demonize other posters. <br /> <br /> <br /> You can't call someone insincere, you aren't reading their mind, that in itself is a personal attack, you have condemned people for much less.<br /> <br /> Cultural groups are not Monoliths I've spoken to people who have stories of Wendigo from their grandparents, and their grandparents would avoid saying the name but would not outright say it is forbidden to refer to the Wendigo. Wendigo and Skinwalkers are not the only beings there are taboos against talking about, many sacred stories in general, like Nunnehi and the like are avoided because there thought to be no need to talk about these things with outsiders, sacred tales of creation were more freely talked about, but its ultimately not a solid line. Aboriginal Tribes in Australia did this as well, and would sometimes tell purposely false tales to better aid in keeping secrets. But you don't speak for a continent of people, even individual communities only speak for themselves. Either don't do a Manitou pantheon or do not complain if they are used.<br /> <br /> And honestly it is less insulting in stories that specifically admit that they are different from the real world because of things like secret histories because there is a layer of separation that you do not get when you try to do a one for one simulation of a subject. Malcom Shepard has talked about this when doing Dragons of the East. A lot of Buddhist stories fit really well into mage, but he felt it would do a disservice to handle it in that way, he grew up buddhist, and so he added a layer of of reconceptualizing for the setting rather then just saying the Buddhist Jatakas and parables are all true and exactly how it handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T01:20:41-07:00","id":1405505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405503#post1405503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it should be noted that the Manitou pantheon was written with the help of members of the Algonquin people, and the writer is himself a Native, Lakota specifically and friends with members of the Algonquin who he called upon to help with the project. So it\u2019s not really disrespectful, because it was made with the help and assistance of the people the topic is important to. It also helps a lot that it doesn\u2019t perpetuate harmful stereotypes of Native peoples</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I am aware, and Mage 20 also made a lot of attempts at handling things in a similar manner, but again Native Americans are not a monolith, you can't just say if I get &quot;insert minority here&quot; then I can speak for the whole group, it just means an attempt was made to handle things respectfully and with fidelity.<br /> <br /> And and there have been bullying of those that aren't minorities, that is the insinuation that well Astromancer is white he isn't allowed to speak his opinion on a subject whether it is broad or narrow because he disagrees with people that outnumber him. the same thing happened to another guy in an older thread about an alternate setting with Greek Roman gods taking over. And several minorities here are ignored or assumptions are cast on them if they do not agree. I've talked with other brown people born on another continent and its insulting when you assume someone is European/White/North American because they disagree with you, especially when its a white posters calling a minority poster white inaccurately.<br /> <br /> This forum has literally gatekeeped people away because if someone disagrees or if someone is a new poster they are mobbed and insulted and false flagged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T01:21:49-07:00","id":1405506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405498#post1405498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because people here constantly bully others who dare to disagree with them here. I am pointing out the fallacy in the logic here. And if you guys don't get CTPhips you will try to go over his head and get Mods that agree with you to contradict him. The rules are simple don't thread crap. If you don't like the idea of this thread then don't thread crap just don't interact with it. You are insulting and mudslinging someone, and when someone points it out you accuse that person of breaking the rules. This is why ideally we have mod arbitration, because you can't just dogpile on someone you disagree with. If you don't like the basic premise of this thread you are not allowed to dogpile it. He says you would freely kick human rights to the curb because in his opinion you would. You can't selectively just declare your insults as not insulting because its true, but who you are disagreeing with is &quot;objectively wrong&quot; so they are insulting. How is this not gatekeeping? If the logic here is Werewolf is wrong, then why aren't you trying to cancel it? By the time we reach revised and W20 they fixed things, there is rich lore, and if someone wants to do a game like that its their right. You can't try to ban people because they disagree with you. You can't ban Astromancer when he is actually engaging with the original poster of the thread and you guys are engaging negatively with the very premise of the thread. This happens all the time here and it is not right. People here bully people for not being minorities but then turn around and bully minorities for not agreeing with them, that is inappropriate. Doing a Manitou Pantheon is just as sacrilegious as other games touching upon the same topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you are feeling bullied, Eldagusto. I mean to criticise ideas here, not people, and I didn't want you to feel personally attacked by what I said.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I have to say that you are, for whatever reason and note that I am just stating my assessment, not accusing you of ill intentions, grieveously misrepresenting the facts here. It was neither Watcher nor Samudra nor Kyman nor Magicjohnny nor I who started to derail this thread. Critian Caceorte presented a project for feedback. They were given feedback, varied feedback by a number of people. Some of that feedback was based on ethical issues in the project as Critian Caceorte presented it, and the derailing started, in my opinion, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403808-scion-x-wta-totem-spirit-pantheon?p=1405217#post1405217\">here</a>, where ethical concerns began to be rejected by a group of Forum users out of hand. None of this, nor the discussion that ensued about ethical issues in general, was bullying, especially not of Critian Caceorte themselves, who has, as all the detractors of Samudra etc. seem to ignore, happily accepted the feedback they were given.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;not getting&quot; CTP; that part of the discussion is still confusing to me, but my ultimate impression was that they overall agree with my position, so even if I were so intrigant as to call upon Mod after Mod until someone does what I want, that would not be necessary in this situation. So I'm not surewhat this line is about.<br /> <br /> I can't speak on the general issues you raise here, the &quot;bullying&quot; and &quot;gatekeeping,&quot; since I'm not on the Forums much anymore, but at least on this thread, that is not the impression I got. The only call for a ban of Astromancer came from Nicolas; that was Nicolas's only post in the thread, and it doesn't reflect on others who have themselves <i>not</i> voiced that call. I will, however, say that I agree with Watcher and Magicjohnny that Astromancer's accusation that Samudra is &quot;violating any and all human rights&quot; (i.e., as Watcher explained, advocating slavery, torture etc.) is both inaccurate and way out of line. Comments like that are, in fact, a case for the Mods, and I see no offense in notifying those about this.<br /> <br /> Lastly, on your claim that the Anishinaabeg Pantheon is sacrilegous in and off itself, I'm not qualified to judge that, since I'm neither Anishinaabe nor an expert on Native North American issues. From your statement, however, I'd wager that neither are you. What I can say is that the Manitou were written by a Native American writer (though not Anishinaabe) in close cooperation with his Anishinaabeg associates, so I think it is the safest playable option of this mythology that we can think of. And this is really all this is about. This is what the ominous &quot;we&quot; you invoke want: A game that is both respectful and fun, that allows us to have fun that doesn't go on another's expense. Scion 2e, by and large, provides that, especially if you look up your details. WtA does not, which is why the initial ethical feedback was offered, since treating the most horrible monster and highest expression of evil in a culture as a fun, harmless patron to play servants of is, in fact, neither respectful nor fun. It is the closest anything mentioned in this thread comes to bullying, namely the bullying of a discriminated group that has suffered genocide by parodying their sacred beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","